\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Higher Vs Yen After BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2000\par 07:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar was higher against the yen in Asian trading Tuesday following the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after warnings made by Japanese monetary authorities early in the session. \par \par \uc2  The euro was slightly lower against the dollar compared with its levels in New York late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to buy dollars for yen when the dollar was trading around Y101.60 and again in the Y102s, pushing up the dollar as high as Y102.75, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  "I think the BOJ spent around $1 billion to $1.5 billion on its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  via Japanese and foreign banks today," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vice minister for international affairs Haruhiko Kuroda confirmed that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market late Tuesday morning to curb the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the session, both Kuroda and his deputy, international bureau head Zembei Mizoguchi, warned that the yen's strengthening is excessive and that the ministry will take proper measures as needed. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  came in the wake of the dollar's fall to Y101.36 in New York late Monday, approaching its 1999 low of Y101.25 and below levels where the BOJ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's rise on Dec. 24. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers noted that the dollar's gains were curbed by Japanese exporters' selling as well as renewed concerns about a possible hike in U.S. interest rates and the potential effect of this on U.S. asset markets. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y102.65, above Y101.65 in New York late Monday. The dollar was quoted at Y101.93 late in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0248, lower than $1.0258 late Monday in New York. The euro was at $1.0169 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Despite the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday, however, the dollar still faces a further downside risk against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  When no major year-2000 computer problems occurred, market players refocused their attention on the next possible market bump: a possible U.S. Federal Reserve interest rate hike, which some say could happen as soon as the next Federal Open Market Committee meeting in February. \par \par \uc2  "The sharp rise in U.S. Treasury yields that spurred the plunge in U.S. stock prices and the fall in the dollar overnight has renewed worries over a potential rate hike at the next FOMC meeting," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Late Monday in New York, the 30-year Treasury Bond yield hit a high of 6.60%, its highest since September 1997. The Dow Jones industrial average finished Monday's session down 139.61 points at 11357.51. \par \par \uc2  While the euro was a little weaker against the dollar in the Asian session, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also seen benefiting from the renewed speculation of a possible U.S. interest rate hike. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro rose in tandem with the dollar's rise, but the euro-yen's upside was capped by offers from Japanese exporters in the Y105s, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was quoted at Y105.20, up from Y104.27 in New York late Monday. The euro was quoted late in Tokyo Monday at Y103.65. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6348, down from $1.6370 in New York late Monday. Sterling was at $1.6201 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Ron Harui; 813-5255-2929; ron.harui@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw14001kv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
