\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Euro in high spirits one year on. \b0\par\par\uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2000\par 07:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 3 (Reuters) - Optimism about Europe's growth \par \par \uc2  prospects in the new year gave the euro a case of deja vu on \par \par \uc2  Monday, helping it celebrate its first trading anniversary in \par \par \uc2  high spirits. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the rally, which lifted the euro\tab     by a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par big figure to highs of around S$1.0185, had been on very light\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par turnover with much of Asia still on holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said trade was likely to remain slow with London also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closed on Monday and as banks remained cautious about potential\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par computer problems despite a smooth crossover to the new year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By early afternoon in Singapore, the euro was off its highs\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but dealers said it showed potential to strengthen in the coming\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weeks as players unwound long dollar positions amid relief over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the lack of major millennium problems.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Last year was not impressive for the euro. But it is the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market view that the euro should rally this year. The assumption\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par is that the U.S. economy will weaken as its stocks are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overvalued," said Thio Chin Loo, strategist at Paribas.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Wim Duisenberg's bullish\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par comments about the euro at the weekend boosted the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar and the yen\tab \tab , dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Duisenberg said he saw upward potential for the euro in 2000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as growth in the euro zone outpaced that in the United States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     EUROPEAN GROWTH SEEN OUTPACING U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We now expect growth in Europe during the course of this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year to be faster than growth in America and that will also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remain in 2001. That is the basic background why we say the euro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has now an upward potential," he said in an interview on Dutch\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Russian President Boris Yeltsin's surprise resignation last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week was also expected to keep the euro supported.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The fact that Yeltsin has gone at last is also seen as a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bonus...the volatility and uncertainty associated with Russia\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could calm down," said Kevin Ralph, first vice president at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sanwa Bank in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers expected the euro to be supported at the previous\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resistance of $1.0185, with a target of $1.0250, ahead of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par December high around $1.0295.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The German purchasing managers' index, due later on Monday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was expected to show continued economic expansion, which in turn\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could spur thoughts of a rate hike.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The market is expecting a 25-basis-point hike in the first\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter of the year, but we would not rule out something more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dramatic," Standard Chartered said in a daily bulletin.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dollar/yen\tab     was slightly pressured by the gains in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par euro/yen, dipping below the 102 level, but activity was very\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par subdued with Japanese markets still shut and lingering wariness\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was little consensus on whether the market would make\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a renewed attempt on the 100 yen level, but dealers expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par caution to prevail ahead of a Group of Seven meeting this month.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0611GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 31 Dec.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0160   1.0070   +0.89   +0.89   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     101.80   102.21   -0.40   -0.40   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    103.54   103.10   +0.43   +0.43   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5785   1.5902   -0.74   -0.74   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6203   1.6176   +0.17   +0.17   1.6176\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4449   1.4455   -0.04   -0.04   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6576   0.6563   +0.20   +0.20   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6062   1.6036   +0.16   +0.16   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6272   0.6239   +0.53   +0.53   0.6239\par \f28 \