\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Euro gains in light early Asian trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 607 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2000\par 02:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 3 (Reuters) - The dollar got off to an \par \par \uc2  extremely quiet start on the first trading day of the new year \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Monday, losing a bit of ground against the euro\tab     and\par holding steady against the yen\tab    .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said business was very slow, with much of Asia\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still out on holiday and banks in the two major centres that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are open -- Hong Kong and Singapore -- keeping a cautious\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stance in the aftermath of the millennium crossover.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "It's very quiet. People are running systems checks and a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lot of people are actually still on holiday," said a trader at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a European bank in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He said there had been some buying of the euro against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar and the yen\tab \tab  following weekend comments by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Wim Duisenberg.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Duisenberg said on Sunday he saw upward potential for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par euro in 2000 as growth in the euro zone outpaced that in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par United States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We now expect growth in Europe during the course of this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year to be faster than growth in America and that will also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remain in 2001. That is the basic background why we say the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par euro has now an upward potential," he said in an interview on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dutch television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the euro's upside was expected to be limited in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par near term, given the lack of overall trading interest.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "A lot of people are bidding on the safe-haven U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because of the millennium concern. Even if (the authorities)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par say all is fine, they want to see that there are really no\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hiccups in settlement," the trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers expect volumes to pick up only in the second week\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of January as most major banks have agreed to limit trade in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par value dates before January 10 to minimise potential computer\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par problems.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Russian President Boris Yeltsin's surprise resignation last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday was also expected to give some support to the euro and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analysts said it could make good headway once the Y2K fears had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par subsided.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Acting President Vladimir Putin has pledged to uphold\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par democratic freedoms and crush attempts at destabilisation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar shed a bit of ground against the yen, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest was very limited with Japan out on holiday and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lingering fears of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  below the 102\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0116GMT. All data taken from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 31 Dec.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0135   1.0070   +0.65   +0.65   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     102.00   102.21   -0.21   -0.21   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    103.44   103.10   +0.33   +0.33   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5835   1.5902   -0.42   -0.42   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6187   1.6176   +0.07   +0.07   1.6176\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4451   1.4455   -0.03   -0.03   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6592   0.6563   +0.44   +0.44   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6070   1.6036   +0.21   +0.21   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6255   0.6239   +0.26   +0.26   0.6239\par     For full report on major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  click on\tab \par     For previous updates on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves click on\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news.....    Debt......\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indicators......\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Reports\tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  All spots....   Europe spots.....\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Volatilities...\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  info from BOJ\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Economic Forecasts......   Official\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates........\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \h