\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro celebrates birthday with strong rally. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 803 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2000\par 23:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 3 (Reuters) - Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  celebrated its first anniversary on Monday with a powerful rally, rising nearly 2 percent against the dollar on stronger European economic news and a sharp decline on Wall Street. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One year after 11 European nations adopted the euro\tab   as a single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the long ailing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  marched higher against both the dollar and yen as traders reported no noteworthy glitches after the millennium date changeover.\par At the close of New York trading, the euro stood at $1.0262, up nearly two cents from its session low while it stood about 1 percent firmer against the yen,\tab      at 104.09. The euro's gains spelled trouble for the greenback, sending it down over half a percent against the yen \tab to 101.56 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Good news from European purchasing managers, whose index soared to its highest level ever at 57.4 in December from 57.0 in November sparked the euro's gains. \par \par \uc2  Buying accelerated dramatically during U.S. trading hours when fears of more U.S. interest rate hikes forced the Dow Jones Industrial Average down 1.21 percent or 139.61 points to 11357.51. \par \par \uc2  Morgan Stanley Dean Witter's U.S. investment strategist Byron Wien helped unhinge trading when he said the Federal Reserve will likely tighten interest rates this spring, taking them up more than a full percentage point by year's end to slow the economy's red-hot pace. \par \par \uc2  Interest rate-sensitive U.S. bonds fell, pushing the yield on the benchmark 30-year Treasury bond up to 6.63 percent, close to its highest level in more than two years. Yields move in the opposite direction of prices. \par \par \uc2  The buying occurred as "people (were) watching the equity have a turnaround," said Seth Garrett, global head of spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Credit Suisse Frist Boston. \par \par \uc2  Later, more buying helped trigger more automatic buying as traders did not want to miss out on the euro's rally. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the morning, a softer-than-expected reading from a key U.S. manufacturing index also helped illustrate the power of Europe's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The closely watched National Association of Purchasing Management's manufacturing sector survey expanded at a slower pace of 55.5 in December after 56.2 in December. \par \par \uc2  "What you see is a signal that (in Europe) manufacturing confidence, at last, has completely caught up with the U.S. and has at this point moved beyond it," said J.P. Morgan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Jim McCormick. \par \par \uc2  Over the weekend, the President of Europe's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wim Duisenberg, who had watched the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lose about 15 percent in value in its first year of trading, promised the euro has room to rise. \par \par \uc2  Bank of France Governor Jean Claude Trichet echoed Duisenberg's comments and traders noted that finally the European policymakers' optimism seemed to have a ring of truth to it. \par \par \uc2  In trading against the yen, the dollar remained down about a half percent from its prior close, but fears about possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cushioned the dollar's decline against the yen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  While previous rounds of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have not clearly halted the dollar's decline, caution prevailed ahead of a meeting of Group of Seven deputy finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors in Japan next week. \par \par \uc2  Traders expressed relief that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading appeared to be going on normally, with so sign of Y2K glitches. Trading had been thin overnight, with most dealers in London and Tokyo off for public holidays. \par \par \uc2  "So far so good," said Grant Wilson, a trader at Mellon Bank in Pittsburgh. "The banks are probably going to play it a bit slow starting off. We'll see how things play out and we'll probably return to normal midweek." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 2213GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    US Close US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab    03 Jan.  31 Dec.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0262   1.0070   +1.91   +0.00   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     101.56   102.21   -0.64   +0.00   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    104.09   103.10   +0.96   +0.00   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5645   1.5902   -1.62   +0.00   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6368   1.6176   +1.19   +0.00   1.6176\par Dlr/can\tab \tab     1.4461   1.4455   +0.04   +0.00   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6579   0.6563   +0.24   +0.00   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6045   1.6036   +0.06   +0.00   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6261   0.6239   +0.35   +0.00   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw1301h1y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
