\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro pares gains but stays well supported. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2000\par 12:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 3 (Reuters) - The euro pared early gains on Monday but began its second year of trading on a generally upbeat note amid growing optimism over an economic pickup in the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  Although the euro failed to sustain its initial rally to two-week highs against the dollar despite robust European purchasing managers surveys, perennial euro bears were wrongfooted as the single curency went off to a positive start after a dismal first year, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "We still haven't seen flows of any substance, but people's view on the euro could change if it sustains its gains from here," said Akira Hoshino, chief trader at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London, adding he himself was still not totally convinced about a reversal. \par \par \uc2  With concerns of possible Y2K computer problems out of the way, focus was shifting to economic fundamentals, which the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had mostly ignored in late 1999. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose more than a cent to a two-week high of $1.0185 in thin Asian trading, bolstered by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg's comments on Sunday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had potential to appreciate. \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg said in an interview on Dutch television he expected European growth this year to be faster than growth in the United States. \par \par \uc2  "It's quite surprising that they are seeing the euro-zone growth outpacing U.S. growth this year," said Eugen Keller, a market strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in Frankfurt, noting that the euro's long-term interest were rising. \par \par \uc2  "Maybe this will open the eyes of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers," he added. \par \par \uc2  Russian President Boris Yeltsin's surprise resignation last week was also expected to keep the euro supported. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that Yeltsin has gone at last is also seen as a bonus...the volatility and uncertainty associated with Russia could calm down," said Kevin Ralph, first vice president at Sanwa Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  In addition, a flurry of European purchasing managers indices were generally supportive of the euro. The euro zone-wide manufacturing PMI rose to 57.4 in December, the highest in survey history, from 57.0 in November. \par \par \uc2  Still, by the time the market got the PMI data, the euro had run out of steam amid a dearth of dealing interest due to a British holiday, leaning against technical support near $1.01. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was broadly softer partly due to unwinding of year-end safe-haven buying, slipping to one-week lows below 102 yen against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Wariness of possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cushioned dollar/yen's decline, traders said. \par \par \uc2  While previous rounds of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have not clearly halted the dollar's decline, caution prevailed ahead of a Group of Seven deputy finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors meeting in Japan next week. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw1301ewc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
