\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar mixed as U.S. markets slide into Y2K. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 779 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 1999\par 19:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NEW YORK, Dec 31 (Reuters) - The dollar slipped against the Japanese yen\tab   in early U.S. afternoon trading, falling victim to last-minute position-squaring in thinned markets as dealers got ready to ring in the year 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With European and Japanese financial markets closed and many U.S. trading desks working with skeletal staffing ahead of the New Year's holiday, extremely limited trading volumes had helped exaggerate the pair's movements, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "There's not much liquidity and even a small amount is going to move the markets these days," said Vincent Palazzolo, chief dealer at Sumitomo Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ticked lower versus the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  before finding footing at its floor for the day near 102.17 yen, down about 0.2 percent from Thursday's close just below 102.40. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said concern that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to staunch the yen's rise, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars for yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last Friday, was helping prop the dollar above 102 yen. \par \par \uc2  Thinned trading conditions also allowed Canadian dollar bulls to trample the greenback. The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied to its highest level for the year at 1.4430 per U.S. dollar, up about half a percent from its prior close. \par \par \uc2  Despite the small flurry of activity, however, most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers were left twiddling their thumbs, watching New Year's celebrations on television, pondering their own plans for the evening - just about anything but dealing. \par \par \uc2  Many U.S. dealers had finished trading early to avoid contracts with a settlement date that would land in the changeover between 1999 and 2000, holding off to see if any Y2K computer bug-related problems occur. \par \par \uc2  "We're just keeping the powder dry. This year is history, so why ruin it?" one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Even the surprise news overnight that Russian President Boris Yeltsin had resigned failed to give the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market any momentum. Yeltsin handed over power to his prime minister, Vladimir Putin. \par \par \uc2  "Surprisingly, even that didn't have any impact because there's just nobody trading: very, very little going through the market right now," said William Bertha, vice president at Mellon Bank in Pittsburgh. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market trading will likely fizzle further shortly after 1:00 p.m. (1800 GMT) when U.S. stock and bond markets ended an abbreviated session and since many bankers plan to head home early, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite the dollar's losses against the yen, it managed to eke out slight gains against Europe's single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . In U.S. afternoon trading, the euro\tab   stood at $1.0060, down about 0.2 percent from Thursday's close of $1.0080.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While Europe's fledgling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held its ground above its session trough, its proximity to lifetime lows below $1.00 reflected the euro's struggles in its tenuous first year of life.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro, which hit its highs soon after its January debut, has fallen about 14 percent against the dollar and about 22 percent versus the yen as concerns over Europe's lagging economic recovery and structural reform clouded its outlook.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We expect that the euro will close the year with a soft tone, and we will not be surprised if that pressure continues on the euro as we start the next year," said Fortis vice president John Schein.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1607)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 1:06 p.m. (1806 GMT).  All data\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par daily U.S. close at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %     1998\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 30 Dec.\tab \tab \tab  Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0060   1.0080   -0.20  -14.17   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     102.18   102.37   -0.19   -9.73   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    103.05   103.13   -0.08  -21.84   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5900   1.5938   -0.24  +15.76   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6150   1.6152   -0.01   -2.35   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4466   1.4530   -0.44   -5.42   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6565   0.6536   +0.44   +7.36   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6053   1.6058   -0.03   -0.41   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6241   0.6236   +0.08  -11.11   0.7021\par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...\tab     Debt...   Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\tab \tab \tab \tab \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \par \par All spots\tab \par Tokyo spots\tab \par Europe spots\tab \par Volatilities\tab \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \