\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar muted in 1999's final trading session. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 764 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 1999\par 17:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Dec 31 (Reuters) - The dollar drifted sideways against Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Japanese yen in early U.S. trading on Friday as U.S. financial markets got set to wrap up the last trading day of the century. \par \par \uc2  With European and Japanese financial market trading already wound down and many U.S. trading desks working with skeletal staffing, the dollar wandered in tight ranges as dealers expected little activity in the hours ahead. \par \par \uc2  While extremely thin year-end trading volumes could make for volatile price action, many dealers were sitting on their hands with little trading to be done. \par \par \uc2  "You will see maybe a wild swing that could be caused by one or two individuals for squaring purposes, and then back to basics," said Fortis vice president John Schein. \par \par \uc2  "By the number of trades we saw yesterday, today is going to be even more restricted," Schein added. \par \par \uc2  Many U.S. dealers had finished up trading early to avoid contracts with a settlement date that would land in the changeover between 1999 and 2000, holding off to see if any Y2K computer bug-related problems occur. \par \par \uc2  And trading will likely fizzle out nearly completely by 1:00 p.m. (1800 GMT) when U.S. stock and bond markets are scheduled to close for the holiday weekend, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After a tiny flurry of activity as New York kicked off its final trading session of 1999, the euro\tab   stood nearly unchanged from Thursday night's close at $1.0080.\par The dollar was similarly stable against the Japanese yen\tab  , winding sideways from its prior close near 102.40.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Even the surprise news overnight that Russian President Boris Yeltsin had resigned failed to give the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market any momentum. Yeltsin handed over power to his prime minister, Vladimir Putin.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Surprisingly, even that didn't have any impact because there's just nobody trading: very, very little going through the market right now," said William Bertha, vice president at Mellon Bank in Pittsburgh.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While Europe's fledgling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  floated near the upper end of its narrow overnight range, its proximity to lifetime lows below $1.00 reflected the euro's struggles in its tenuous first year of life.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro, which hit its highs soon after its January debut, has fallen about 14 percent against the dollar and about 22 percent versus the yen as concerns over Europe's lagging economic recovery and structural reform clouded its outlook.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We expect that the euro will close the year with a soft tone, we will not be surprised if that pressure continues on the euro as we start the next year," said Schein.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the time being, dealers said the market's lack of momentum would keep the euro trapped well below $1.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar drifted near its lows against the yen, but fear that the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the strength of the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would likely keep the dollar propped above the 101.90-102 support area, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BoJ bought dollars for yen in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets last Friday to dampen the ascent of the yen, which Tokyo worries could bite into Japan's nascent economic recovery by lifting the price of Japan's exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1607))\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 10:23 a.m. (1523 GMT).  All data\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par daily U.S. close at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %     1998\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 30 Dec.\tab \tab \tab  Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0080   1.0080   +0.00  -14.00   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     102.39   102.37   +0.02   -9.55   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    103.19   103.13   +0.06  -21.73   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5908   1.5938   -0.19  +15.82   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6145   1.6152   -0.04   -2.38   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4484   1.4530   -0.32   -5.30   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6537   0.6536   +0.02   +6.90   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6046   1.6058   -0.07   -0.45   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6245   0.6236   +0.14  -11.05   0.7021\par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...\tab     Debt...   Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\tab \tab \tab \tab \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \par \par All spots\tab \par Tokyo spots\tab \par Europe spots\tab \par Volatilities\tab \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\tab \par World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  