\par\par \b \uc2  Japan must act if yen rises excessively-BOJ quoted. \b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 1999\par 22:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  must \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the yen rises excessively, domestic daily Yomiuri Shimbun quoted Bank of Japan (BOJ) Governor Masaru Hayami as saying in an interview published on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  Hayami said Japanese corporate profits were growing despite the yen's rise to its current level and that companies were now more able to cope with a strong yen, Yomiuri reported. \par \par \uc2  But he added it would be necessary to respond by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the yen exhibited a one-way rise to higher levels, the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  In a separate interview with Nihon Keizai Shimbun, Hayami said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was always watching carefully to see if the exchange rate was in line with economic fundamentals and would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there was volatility when the market was thin. \par \par \uc2  But he said it was difficult to alter rates greatly through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If the yen weakened because of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japanese exports might increase. But that could run counter to the interests of other countries, so joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not be carried out easily, Nihon Keizai reported. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcv07fps\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
