\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro holds head up as markets head into Y2K. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 766 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1999\par 23:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Dec 30 (Reuters) - Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eked out modest gains on Thursday, but with just one more trading day left in 1999, the euro seemed poised to end its debut year with a whimper. \par \par \uc2  In late New York trading, last-minute position-squaring had helped rescue the euro after it keeled toward its lows earlier in the session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We pulled the rubberband a little bit and it's just snapping back," said Ben Strauss, vice president at Bank Julius Baer. \par \par \uc2  The euro finished Thursday trading at $1.0080, up nearly 0.4 percent from $1.0043 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  But with skeleton staffing on many bank trading desks ahead of the New Year weekend creating extremely thin trading conditions, the euro was unable to gain much momentum, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe's fledgling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab   was left dangling less than a cent away from its lifetime lows against the dollar below $1.00 and about one yen above its all-time trough versus the Japanese yen near 102 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said they anticipated even less action in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets on Friday, when stock and bond markets will close early at 1:00 p.m. (1800 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro's year-end weakness only accentuated a sobering first year in which it slumped 14 percent against the dollar, 22 percent against the yen and around 12 percent against the pound.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The euro is sitting where it was two weeks ago, which is probably a disappointing result given the continued strong cyclical data out of the region," McCormick said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro's first year was initially marred by Europe's slow economic recovery and later by concerns over structural problems in the region's economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar, meanwhile has outperformed the euro, as the U.S. economy continues to post astonishing growth rates and America's seemingly unstoppable stock markets cruise to record highs as the millennium wanes.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar's strength against European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was reflected as it very briefly rose above 1.60 Swiss francs\tab  , touching a 10-year high against the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1.6010 before retreating to end the day softer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight, the market had already begun to shrug off economic data and verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by monetary authorities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro barely moved after European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board member Tommaso Padoa-Schioppa reiterated that the euro was underestimated, echoing his comments and similar comments from other ECB and Bundesbank officials made on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It also ignored a fall in the French unemployment rate to 10.8 percent in November from 11.0 percent in October and Italian November producer prices, up 2.2 percent year-on-year - the steepest rise since April 1996.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the yen\tab  , the dollar edged modestly higher to finish at 102.37, up 0.2 percent from 102.15 on Wednesday. Fears the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb export-crippling yen strength, as it did last week, have capped the robust yen from rising further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In a bid to allay fear of any Y2K funding squeeze, the Bank of Japan left a staggering 22.6 trillion yen net surplus in the money market - more than 20 times the already accommodative one-trillion-yen surplus it had been leaving in the market for months until last week to keep overnight call rates near zero.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But yen was unfazed by the extra fund injection as the move was seen as a temporary, technical Y2K measure and not a sign of further easing in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 2202GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab US Close US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1998\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Cls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab 30 Dec.  29 Dec.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0080   1.0043   +0.37  -14.32   1.1721\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab     102.37   102.15   +0.22   -9.76   113.20\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    103.13   102.62   +0.50  -22.16   131.84\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5938   1.5972   -0.21  +16.29   1.3735\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6152   1.6170   -0.11   -2.23   1.6539\par  Dlr/can\tab \tab     1.4530   1.4527   +0.02   -5.02   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab   0.6536 0.6508 +0.43 +6.43 0.6115 Euro/swiss 1.6058 1.6049 +0.06 -0.43 1.6119 Euro/stg\tab      0.6236 0.6209 +0.43 -11.57 0.7021\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1607)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcu07esv\par }\page 