\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro sways above life lows as 1999 winds down. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Daniel Sternoff \par \uc2 807 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1999\par 16:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Dec 30 (Reuters) - Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  waffled just above its all-time lows on Thursday, approaching the end of its first year of trading substantially weaker against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab   hung barely a quarter cent above parity to the dollar in anaemic New York trading thinned by Y2K settlement risk, with its $0.9986 historic floor lurking below.\par Against the Japanese yen\tab     , the bruised euro dangled just over half a yen above its 102.03 all-time low, and floated above 62 pence, just a whisker above a lifetime trough against the British pound   .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Dealers in half-staffed trading rooms said activity was primarily limited to year-end balance sheet adjustments, with the bruised euro bearing the brunt of last minute position adjustments. \par \par \uc2  "It is difficult to know if this is a trend we should worry about because there aren't a lot of trades going through," said Jim McCormick, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan. \par \par \uc2  European and Japanese dealers have mainly wrapped up the year and many U.S. traders have stopped taking orders as players shun contracts straddling the date change from 1999 to 2000, waiting to see how computers cope with the Y2K bug. \par \par \uc2  But the euro's year-end weakness only accentuated a sobering first year in which it slumped 14 percent against the dollar, 22 percent against the yen and around 12 percent against the pound. \par \par \uc2  "The euro is sitting where it was two weeks ago, which is probably a disappointing result given the continued strong cyclical data out of the region," McCormick said. \par \par \uc2  The euro's first year was initially marred by Europe's slow economic recovery and later by concerns over structural problems in the region's economy. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, meanwhile has outperformed the euro, as the U.S. economy continues to post astonishing growth rates and America's seemingly unstoppable stock markets cruise to record highs as the millennium wanes. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar's strength against European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was reflected as it very briefly rose above 1.60 Swiss francs\tab  , touching a 10-year high against the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1.6010 before retreating.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With no inclination to take speculative positions now, the market paid little heed overnight to economic data or verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by monetary authorities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro barely moved after European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board member Tommaso Padoa-Schioppa reiterated that the euro was underestimated, echoing his comments and similar comments from other ECB and Bundesbank officials made on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It also ignored a fall in the French unemployment rate to 10.8 percent in November from 11.0 percent in October and Italian November producer prices, up 2.2 percent year-on-year - the steepest rise since April 1996.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the yen\tab   the dollar was little changed above 102 yen. Fears the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb export-crippling yen strength, as it did last week, have capped the robust yen from rising further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In a bid to allay fear of any Y2K funding squeeze, the Bank of Japan left a staggering 22.6 trillion yen net surplus in the money market - more than 20 times the already accommodative one-trillion-yen surplus it had been leaving in the market for months until last week to keep overnight call rates near zero.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But yen was unfazed by the extra fund injection as the move was seen as a temporary, technical Y2K measure and not a sign of further easing in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212 859 1690)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 10:04 a.m. (1504 GMT).  All data taken\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %    1998\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 29 Dec.\tab \tab \tab  Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0038   1.0043   -0.05  -14.36   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     102.25   102.15   +0.10   -9.67   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    102.52   102.62   -0.10  -22.24   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5980   1.5972   +0.05  +16.35   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6150   1.6170   -0.12   -2.35   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4530   1.4527   +0.02   -5.00   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6529   0.6508   +0.32   +6.77   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6044   1.6049   -0.03   -0.47   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6209   0.6209   +0.00  -11.57   0.7021\par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...\tab     Debt...   Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Curr