\par\par \b \uc2  Japan spent record sums in 1999 to push down yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1999\par 11:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 30 (Reuters) - Japan spent a record high of $69.33 billion in 1999 trying to prevent its high-flying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from imperiling a nascent economic recovery, bankers estimated on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Thursday showed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) paid 1.5580 trillion yen ($15.27 billion) to the private sector in December through its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account. \par \par \uc2  Bankers analysing the data estimated that $15.12 billion represented \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the one-month period from November 29 to December 28. \par \par \uc2  As a result, traders and analysts believe the year-end total to have hit a record high, surpassing an estimated $49.0 billion worth of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted during 1995, when the yen rose to a record high of 79.75 yen. \par \par \uc2  Japan has often gone it alone in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market trying to keep the yen from strengthening. \par \par \uc2  A stronger yen reduces the value of overseas earnings by Japan's big export-oriented companies. \par \par \uc2  Officials worry that any fresh drag could stop the economy from coming out of its worst recession since the end of World War Two. \par \par \uc2  The yen has been rising since April when it was at 127 to the dollar due to a rush into Tokyo shares by international investors. \par \par \uc2  Japan has had to spend record sums partly because of the reluctance of its Group of Seven (G7) economic allies to join in. \par \par \uc2  Foreign officials have said that Japan has not done enough to reform the economy so that it can have a self-sustaining recovery and has failed to ensure that the record amounts of cash in the banking system encourages fresh lending by banks. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was detected conducting yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January, June, July, September, November and December this year. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ acts as an agent for the MOF and conducts actual dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  through transactions with brokers and private banks. \par \par \uc2  The MOF has confirmed that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen, using the BOJ as an agent, on November 29 and November 30. Bankers said the BOJ was also detected buying euros against the yen on both dates. \par \par \uc2  Besides \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , MOF's disbursements also include financial transactions between \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and global institutions such as the International Monetary Fund. ((Masayuki Kitano, Tokyo Treasury Desk \par \par \uc2  +81-3-5473-3748 tokyo newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcu07e72\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
