\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Nov,Dec dlr buys around $15.12 bln-bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1999\par 11:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 30 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan (BOJ) spent an estimated $15.12 billion buying dollars through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a one-month period from November 29 to Tuesday this week, bankers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  As a result, the estimated amount of the BOJ's buying of dollars and euros against the yen for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1999 rose to a total of $69.33 billion. \par \par \uc2  Traders and analysts believe the amount to be a record high, surpassing an estimated $49.0 billion worth of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted during 1995, when the yen rose to a record high of 79.75 yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was detected conducting yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January, June, July, September, November and December this year. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Thursday showed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) paid 1.5580 trillion yen to the private sector in December through its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, which mostly represents \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ acts as an agent for the MOF and conducts actual dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  through transactions with brokers and private banks. \par \par \uc2  The MOF has confirmed that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen, using the BOJ as an agent, on November 29 and November 30. Bankers said the BOJ was also detected buying euros against the yen on both dates. \par \par \uc2  The MOF has also confirmed that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen on December 24. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 102.07 yen as of 1005 GMT, compared with 102.15 yen in late U.S. trading on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at 102.52 yen against 102.62 yen in late U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2  Besides \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , MOF's disbursements also include financial transactions between \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and global institutions such as the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  The figures include the last two trading days of the previous month, but not the last two business days of the month, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlements are made two days after transactions. \par \par \uc2      A breakdown of the estimated amounts of the BOJ's yen-selling \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1999 are as follows: (in billions of dollars) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Month:\tab     Amount :\tab \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :\par     January\tab    6.74\tab     dollar\par     June\tab      25.65\tab     dollar, euro\par     July\tab      12.11\tab     dollar\par     September\tab  9.71\tab     dollar\par     November and   15.12\tab     dollar, euro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     December\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TOTAL:\tab    69.33\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-5473-3748\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcu07e6i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100