\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar steers even keel as market eyes Y2K. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1999\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 29 (Reuters) - Major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked well-worn ranges in thin volume on Wednesday, as many investors steered clear of trading ahead of the millennium, analysts and dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Settlement for spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  contracts moved to January from December on Wednesday, making investors cautious to trade because of concern about potential Y2K problems. \par \par \uc2  "We've been trading in very narrow ranges," said David Coleman, chief economist at CIBC World Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  "We're in the awkward bit in the middle between Christmas and New Year, and there is unlikely to be much serious business done in the next couple of days." \par \par \uc2  The euro trod water within one cent of the psychological one-for-one level with the dollar, hamstrung by strength in both U.S. and European stock markets. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average rose to a record close on Tuesday, while the German DAX hit its tenth successive record close on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "There are lots of things which should help the euro next year," said Coleman. \par \par \uc2  "European markets are looking better value than North American markets. Investors are looking for value and Europe is probably one of the best places to be." \par \par \uc2  The market showed negligible reaction to comments by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice President Christian Noyer in French newspaper Liberation that the euro had strong potential to appreciate and he was personally not happy with the euro's fall. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market was becoming immune to such remarks and was unlikely to believe the ECB would take any imminent actions to reverse the euro's year-long weakness. \par \par \uc2  The euro also ignored data showing the euro-zone January-October trade surplus was 83.3 billion euros compared with 98.4 billion a year ago. Italian December retail inflation pushed above two percent to its highest 1999 rate, but national statistics office ISTAT said full-year CPI should still come in at a tamer 1.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR HOLDS 102 YEN \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was also stuck in a narrow range above 102 yen as the 102-area had proved to be good support in the last few days amid wariness of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's export-crippling ascent. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody wants to get far from the 102.00-102.50 yen range today," said a Japanese trust bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that although activity was likely to dry up as the year-end approached, the BOJ could step into the market whenever thin volume exaggerated price fluctuations, or at least offer verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ does have a tendency to talk the yen down in thin, illiquid trading conditions," said Coleman. "We could certainly see some chat from Japanese officials in the next few days." \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's resolve to counter any Y2K-related disruptions was apparent in a record 14.6 trillion yen surplus it left in the Japanese money market on Tuesday, up from an already extraordinary 9.1 trillion on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said different settlement dates for spot dollar/yen and euro/yen contracts, generally January 4 for the former and January 3 for the latter, heightened market participants' reluctance to trade. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvct07hx6\par