\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dlr stalled above Y102, little activity seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 868 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1999\par 08:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 29 (Reuters) - The dollar stood at a standstill above 102 yen in late Tokyo trade on Wednesday, a level little changed from late New York, as Y2K-related liquidity risk kept many Japanese banks sidelined, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  With the settlement date for spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  contracts now in January, few customers wanted to trade. Those who did want to trade on spot basis had done so by Tokyo's 0100 GMT local fixing, when the dollar hit an intraday high of 102.50 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Scattered dollar selling, aimed at unwinding yen-short positions ahead of the year-end, was detected by a few foreign operators in Tokyo afternoon trading. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody wants to get far from the 102.00-102.50 yen range today," said a Japanese trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As of 0635 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 102.30/35 yen\tab  , compared with 102.35 in New York late on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The threat of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (BOJ) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has provided solid support at 102.00 yen, while Japanese exporters were still thought to have offers around 102.80 and 103.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said although activity is highly likely to dry up as the year-end approaches, the BOJ is expected to step into the market whenever thin volumes exaggerate price fluctuations and result in the dollar's sharp fall versus the yen, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The BOJ seems to be prepared for unexpected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements, especially today and tomorrow. That's because, for example, one exporter sell order could result in a sudden drop amid a lack of participants," said a U.S. bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro steadied at $1.0077/84 after skidding almost a cent at one stage overnight to around $1.0035. It ended in New York at $1.0069 on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The weakness was attributed in part to a hiccup in the German government's plans to abolish a tax on proceeds from the sale of corporate cross shareholdings.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The plan has fuelled a surge in the German equity market but now the main opposition party has come out against the proposal and there are reports that some within the ruling party were also uncomfortable with it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dollar sentiment, meanwhile, was supported by further robust U.S. economic data showing consumer confidence has risen to a 31-year high.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wall Street also ended at an all-time high on Tuesday, marking a gain for the year of 25 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some dealers said they are concerned about the fate of a Japanese plan to introduce the so-called "payoff" limited deposit guarantee scheme.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If the start of the plan is delayed as Japanese media reported on Wednesday, that could undermine the yen. But many others said that a delay itself would not stop capital from flowing into Japan over the mid-to longer-term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Unlike in the past, the delay of the payoff plan would not trigger fears over the Japanese banking system," said another trust bank dealer. "Bank shares may be sold, but as long as other shares continue attracting foreigners, that would keep the yen sentiment buoyant."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has proposed the full guarantee of bank deposits now provided by the government be replaced in April 2001 by a new safety net scheme, the so-called payoff system, guaranteeing a maximum of 10 million yen per depositor in the event of bank failures.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But calls are increasing among leading coalition party politicians for delaying the start of the new scheme in the run-up to a general election due in less than a year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier on Wednesday, the BOJ left a record 14.6 trillion yen in the money market via its regular \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , up from an already huge 9.1 trillion on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the market was unfazed by increased surplus left in the money market for a fifth consecutive business day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ has made it clear that this is aimed at subduing any upward pressure related to the millennium computer bug on key unsecured overnight call rate, the rate it guides through its open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and is not a further easing in its already relaxed monetary policy. ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0726 GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1998 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   28 Dec.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0077   1.0069   +0.08   -14.03   1.1721\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      102.20   102.35   -0.15    -9.72   113.20\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     103.00   103.03   -0.03   -21.88   131.84\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.5924   1.5943   -0.12   +15.94   1.3735\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.6158   1.6143   +0.09    -2.30   1.6539\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4510   1.4500   +0.07    -5.13   1.5295\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6462   0.6460   +0.03    +5.67   0.6115\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6047   1.6057   -0.06    -0.45   1.6119\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6236   0.6230   +0.10   -11.18   0.7021.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvct07gbp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
