\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro ends softer as markets gear up for Y2K. \b0\par\par\uc2 773 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1999\par 23:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Dec 29 (Reuters) - Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sagged broadly on Wednesday as dealers snubbed the year-old unit in thinned trading conditions in the days leading to the millennium changeover weekend. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In late New York trading, the euro\tab   hung at session lows against the dollar, less a half a cent above one-on-one parity with the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and down about 0.3 percent from Tuesday's close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "The market is intent on taking (the euro) below parity and that's going to be the bias ahead of year-end and probably early next week as well," said David Gilmore, partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The fledgling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had also earlier slipped to one-week lows against the Japanese yen\tab   and came briefly within striking distance of its lifetime low against the the British pound, below 62 pence.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the euro's slide failed to gather steam as trading slowed to a trickle late in the New York session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Many traders said they had stopped taking orders, shunning spot trades conducted Wednesday that would settle early next week, when markets discover how time-sensitive computer systems have weathered the date change from 1999 to 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We're in Y2K shutdown mode," said Rick Gomes, managing director of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at Republic National Bank of New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said speculative players were sidelined and activity was limited to customers who had no choice but to settle monthly or annual accounts before year's end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen's gains against the euro buoyed it against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as well, pushing the dollar briefly below key support near 102 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But dealers said concern the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again to curb the yen's rise after it sold yen on Friday capped the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's gains, and the dollar\tab   pared its losses to stand near 102.15 yen in late New York trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Many dealers ignored the market's modest swings, saying they were more focused on readying their trading systems for the century change.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We are trying to encourage customers to settle for January 10 and avoid settling the first week," Gomes said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If they want to trade for the 3rd or 4th, we'll do it, but we're trying to minimise the number of transactions settling for the 3rd or 4th until we get through the Y2K hump." he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight, the market was oblivious to attempts by European central bankers to talk up the euro as it approaches its first anniversary some 14 percent weaker against the dollar and around 22 percent softer against the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  council member Tommaso Padoa-Schioppa told the French newspaper Le Monde on Wednesday the euro's fundamentals were underestimated, while ECB Vice President Christian Noyer told the French newspaper Liberation the euro had room to rise and he was personally not happy with its fall.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "All that's been said is just a repeat of what we have seen in the past," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic advisor at Bank of America in London.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Separately, Bundesbank council member Franz-Christoph Zeitler said in a statement that government plans to scrap a tax on sales of Germany's web of domestic cross shareholdings could help boost the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Doubts the plans would ever be implemented kept the euro a full cent below highs reached last Thursday, analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen, meanwhile was unfazed by a staggering 14.6 trillion yen surplus the Bank of Japan left in the Japanese money market - following a massive 9.1 trillion surplus a day earlier - to counter any Y2K-disruptions.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 2209GMT.  All data taken from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuterswith percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US Close US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1998\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 29 Dec.  28 Dec.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0043   1.0069   -0.26  -14.09   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     102.15   102.35   -0.20   -9.58   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    102.62   103.03   -0.40  -21.85   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5972   1.5943   +0.18  +16.08   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6170   1.6143   +0.17   -2.39   1.6539\par Dlr/can\tab \tab     1.4527   1.4500   +0.19   -5.20   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6508   0.6460   +0.74   +5.64   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6049   1.6057   -0.05   -0.38   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6209   0.6230   -0.34  -11.27   0.7021\par \f28 \pa