\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Slightly Down Vs Yen Ahead Of Year-End \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 1999\par 06:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar was slightly lower against the yen in Asian trading Tuesday, though the dollar's downside was limited by fears of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro was marginally higher against the dollar compared with late Monday's New York levels. Euro trading was thin as many market players were reluctant to trade due to Tuesday's holiday in the United Kingdom. \par \par \uc2  Some Japanese banks sold dollars for yen on behalf of investment trust funds looking to hedge or liquidate their foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated assets, which pushed the dollar down, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The selling came in the wake of dollar-supportive comments from a top official at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday morning, dealers noted. \par \par \uc2  Early in the session, Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said that the yen's current strengthening is excessive and added that the ministry is always watching \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  carefully. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda's comments made market players more fearful of possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's strength last Friday. \par \par \uc2  Such fears may have sparked unconfirmed rumors that the BOJ was checking \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates this morning, which also helped to push up the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, some dealers attributed the dollar's rise to strong dollar demand related to the Tokyo fixing at 0100 GMT. Tuesday is the last trading day for settlement this year. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y102.24, below Y102.39 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at Y102.62 late Monday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0138, higher than $1.0130 late Monday in New York. The euro was at $1.0133 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y103.65, down from Y103.72 in New York late Monday. The euro was at Y103.98 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6166, down from $1.6173 in New York late Monday. Sterling was at $1.6166 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Market participants mostly shrugged off the Bank of Japan's very generous money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday morning, which left a record Y9.1 trillion above the reserves requirement. \par \par \uc2  "There was no impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from the BOJ's money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  this morning as it was perceived as an effort to counter year-end funding pressure," said a dealer at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  Although a BOJ official said that these excess reserves "included funds spent for (the BOJ's) yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday," the official added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't think in terms of whether this represents unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  money. \par \par \uc2  The official also said the BOJ would gradually drain some of the excess funds after the new year. \par \par \uc2  According to market players, BOJ sold less than Y100 billion against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Friday in its effort to weaken the yen. That money is due for settlement this session. \par \par \uc2  Remarks from Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa Tuesday also failed to stir the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. He said that he told officials at his ministry to be cautious about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  conditions as the end of the year approaches. He noted that the market is usually thin at the year end and this year in particular, there are fears about possible Y2K computer problems. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro stayed trapped in a narrow range in the Asian session as many market players were sidelined. \par \par \uc2  "The year-end is approaching and the United Kingdom is on holiday today, so market players are refraining from trading the euro aggressively at this time," said a dealer at a Japanese trust bank. \par \par \uc2  -By Ron Harui; 813-5255-2929; rharui@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvcs08mr4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
