\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen backtracks, holds modest ranges. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 1999\par 14:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 28 (Reuters) - The buoyant yen backtracked slightly on Tuesday after a brief rally on sporadic year-end corporate demand as wariness of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  subdued follow-through buying. \par \par \uc2  The to-and-fro movement was amplified by reluctance among price-making banks to take on fresh positions ahead of the year-end due to Y2K concerns, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "This is the last day of trading for spot settlement this year, which means you're getting some flows from people who want to get stuff done before the year-end," said Johnathan Bayley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Paribas in Paris. "But there doesn't seem to be any strong underlying sentiment either way." \par \par \uc2  "That's why you don't really have a lot of movement, but when you do get a movement, it's the result of corporate orders going through in an illiquid market," he added. \par \par \uc2  An absence of actual BOJ yen selling, expectations the Japanese economy would continue to recover next year and that Tokyo stocks would extend gains initially supported the yen, taking dollar/yen JPY=) to a session low near 102 yen early in Europe from the highs in Asia around 102.70. \par \par \uc2  By European midday, however, the dollar had clawed back up toward the middle of that range, which was also the middle of a relatively tight 101.20-103.80 monthly range for December. \par \par \uc2  Michael Rottmann, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HypoVereinsbank in Munich, said the dollar's range-trading with some downward bias was likely to continue until the next meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers to be held in Japan in January. \par \par \uc2  "We still believe that the low end of the range is somewhere between 101 and 102, more or less based on fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the upper end should be between 103 and 104," he said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day, the yen weathered the BOJ's decision to leave a staggering 9.1 trillion net surplus in the Japanese money market, more than twice Monday's 4.5 trillion yen, which itself was a record. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ said the surplus was boosted to prevent Y2K pressures from inflating the key overnight rate, which it has long kept around 0.02 percent. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo dealers said the huge surplus blurred the argument over "unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", in which the BOJ leaves extra yen funds in the private sector resulting from its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to subdue demand for yen. The BOJ has long argued such a policy is meaningless. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, dealers found it hard to see what difference it would make by leaving Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised when the transactions settled today, as it probably amounted to a couple of billion yen amid an overall surplus of nine trillion. \par \par \uc2  "You can't even spot it amongst all this liquidity," said a dealer at a European bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro EUR=) treaded water in a very tight range above $1.01. \par \par \uc2  The euro's sentiment was supported by generally improving economic fundamentals and some progress on the structural front, including the German government's tax reform proposal unveiled last week. \par \par \uc2  Eugen Keller, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fixed income strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in Frankfurt, added that short-term traders' overwhelmingly bearish view on the euro - in contrast to their bullish views a year ago - could from a contrarian standpoint be a sign the euro was set to appreciate next year. \par \par \uc2  European economic data were scarce, and the euro hardly reacted to euro zone money supply data. The area's 12-month M3 growth accelerated to 6.2 percent in November against 5.8 percent in October, in line with market expectations. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  directorate member Tommaso Padoa-Schioppa was quoted by Germany weekly Die Welt as saying clear signs of structural reforms in Germany and Italy would help the euro strengthen. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcs07jqw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
