\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen stays buoyant in absence of BOJ action. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 1999\par 09:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 28 (Reuters) - The yen remained broadly buoyant on Tuesday, quickly recovering early losses amid persistent year-end commercial demand in the absence of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Expectations the Japanese economy would continue to recover next year and Tokyo stocks would extend gains underpinned bullish sentiment on the yen, although wariness of BOJ action kept dollar/yen well inside a relatively tight monthly range between 101.20 and 103.80 yen for December. \par \par \uc2  Michael Rottmann, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HypoVereinsbank in Munich, said the dollar's range-trading with some downward bias would likely continue until the next meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers to be held in Japan in January. \par \par \uc2  "Until then, the MOF (\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) and the BOJ will cap pressures on the downside, but this won't change the trend," he said. "We still believe that the low end of the range is somewhere between 101 and 102, more or less based on fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the upper end should be between 103 and 104." \par \par \uc2  The greenback did briefly hop as high as 102.70 yen in Asia as a few buy orders made a big splash in a very illiquid market. That in turn stirred talk of BOJ involvement, but dealers were sceptical and the dollar quickly faded below 102.50. \par \par \uc2  With the year's business drawing to a close, order flows appeared to be dominated by last-minute commercial yen buying, namely repatriation of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  receipts by Japanese exporters into yen, and some hedging activity. \par \par \uc2  The yen easily weathered the BOJ's decision to leave a staggering 9.1 trillion net surplus in the money market, more than twice Monday's 4.5 trillion yen, which itself was a record. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ said the surplus was boosted to prevent Y2K pressures from inflating the key overnight rate, which it has long kept around 0.02 percent. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo dealers said the huge surplus blurred the argument over "unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", in which the BOJ leaves extra yen funds in the private sector resulting from its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to subdue demand for yen. The BOJ has long argued such a policy is meaningless. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, dealers found it hard to see what difference it would make by leaving Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised when the transactions settled today, as it probably amounted to a couple of billion yen amid an overall surplus of nine trillion. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is small beer," said a dealer at a European bank. "You can't even spot it amongst all this liquidity." \par \par \uc2  Today's helping of Japanese economic data was again too mixed to provide direction for the market. \par \par \uc2  The unemployment rate dipped rather unexpectedly to 4.5 percent in November from 4.6 percent. But the Tokyo consumer price index which showed a steep 1.5 pct fall year-on-year in December, the biggest drop since 1971, while wage earner's spending fell a real 2.4 pct year/year in November. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro was stuck in a very tight band around $1.0130 and traders saw little prospect of a breakout given the London market was still off for a bank holiday. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, the euro's sentiment was underpinned by further gains in the German share market which has boomed since last week on a government proposal to abolish a tax on company sales of cross shareholdings. \par \par \uc2  European economic data were scarce, and a downward revision in October pan-German output index to 107.4 from 107.6 triggered virtually no reaction in the euro exchange rates. ((London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcs07ipj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
