\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Drops Slightly Vs Yen In Thin Market \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hidenobu Kageyama \par \uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 1999\par 06:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar was slightly down Monday in thin Asian trading, but its floor was firm amid fear that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dropped as low as Y102.62 at one stage compared to Y102.75 late Friday in London. U.S. financial markets were closed for the Christmas holiday Friday. \par \par \uc2  While the dollar managed to rise as high as Y103.00 in the Asian morning as demand was seen around the Tokyo retail fixing, any further upward moves were thwarted. \par \par \uc2  "Offers from exporters capped the dollar's potential rise above Y103.00," said Kazuki Fujita, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at the Industrial Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  Later in the day, it was the Japanese exporters again who sold the dollar to its intraday low in otherwise thin trading. \par \par \uc2  "While the amount was not considerable, exporters continued selling the dollar," Fujita added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials again warned against further yen strength Monday morning, saying the yen is still excessively strong against the dollar and euro and that the ministry will continue carefully monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves even over holidays. \par \par \uc2  Market participants largely ignored those remarks, but added that if the dollar were to fall below Y102.00, the BOJ could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest a further dollar drop. \par \par \uc2  Last Friday the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the dollar when it saw the dollar hovering just below Y102, dealers said. Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda confirmed the action later that day. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y102.62, below Y102.75 late Friday in London. The dollar was at Y102.85 late Friday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0133, lower than $1.0150 late Friday in London. The euro was at $1.0127 in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y103.98, down from Y104.30 in London late Friday. The euro was at Y104.16 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6166, down from $1.6218 in London late Friday. Sterling was at $1.6155 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The euro's moves against the dollar were also limited in Asian trading. The euro was confined to a narrow range between $1.0120 and $1.0140 with a dearth of trading incentives. \par \par \uc2  Trading is likely to stay subdued in light of Monday's national holiday in the United Kingdom, dealers said. Monday is also a national holiday in Australia, New Zealand and Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro traded narrowly as well, in a range between Y103.95 and Y104.35. \par \par \uc2  "In tandem with the dollar/yen, the euro slightly slipped to Y103.95 on offers from Japanese exporters," a senior trader at a Japanese bank said. \par \par \uc2  But fear of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented further euro losses against the yen, traders added. \par \par \uc2  The euro will likely be consolidated in a range between $1.0100-$1.0200 during the rest of 1999, but many Tokyo traders noted the euro might fall against the dollar in tandem with any firms moves in the U.S. stock market next year. \par \par \uc2  "I think the euro's weak tone might be extended early next year on expected strong moves in the U.S. stocks," a senior dealer at a Japanese trust bank said. \par \par \uc2  -By Hidenobu Kageyama; 813-5255-2929; hidenobu.kageyama@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvcr08lqt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
