\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar easier in lifeless Tokyo trade. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Masayuki Kitano \par \uc2 878 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 1999\par 04:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 27 (Reuters) - The dollar was easier against the yen by late morning on Monday in thin trade dominated by customer flows, as calm returned to the market after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last week. \par \par \uc2  The yen hardly budged, despite the Bank of Japan's decision to leave a record 4.5 trillion yen surplus in the money market, and showed muted reaction to a 3.8 percent month-on-month rise in industrial output in November. \par \par \uc2  The dollar initially edged lower due to sporadic selling by Japanese exporters, but later regained some ground due to dollar buying by Japanese importers. \par \par \uc2  As most banks were refraining from trading for their own accounts, trading was thin and there was potential for choppy movements, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There is hardly any dealing activity going on. Moves are dictated by customer flows. As a result, the market is pretty thin and can move quickly even if the flows are not large," said a senior dealer for a city bank. \par \par \uc2  But overall, moves were subdued, and the dollar was stuck in a narrow range between 102.67 yen and 103.00 yen on Monday morning. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar\tab   stood at 102.70/77 yen as of 0232 GMT against 102.89 yen in late U.S. trading on Friday.\par The euro\tab   was quoted at $1.0126/33 against $1.0128 in late U.S. trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market will be closed from Thursday until trade resumes on January 4.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance Ministry officials were not letting down their guard, however, and reiterated their resolve to take action if necessary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Senior MOF official Zembei Mizoguchi said Japan will deal with disruptive movements in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets which could occur in thin year-end conditions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs, Haruhiko Kuroda said the yen is still too strong against the dollar and the euro, but declined to comment on the possibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asked whether the Japanese monetary authorities intend to conduct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday as they did on Friday, Kuroda told reporters at the ministry: "I will not comment on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But he reiterated that the yen's rise has been excessive and said it remained too strong against the dollar and the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said wariness of further yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would increase if the dollar was to fall below 102 yen, which is around where the Bank of Japan was initially detected buying dollars on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the near term, there may be some focus on the Bank of Japan's money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday, when settlement of the BOJ's dollar buying, yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday is due.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said some overseas players were focusing on whether the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will absorb and "sterilise" the excess funds in the market stemming from its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , or leave it in the market "unsterilised".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The latter step was advocated by former MOF official Eisuke Sakakibara on Sunday, when he said on a television programme that the BOJ should not sterilise Friday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But some traders said the sterilisation debate was meaningless at the moment given the record fund surplus left in the money market by the BOJ on Monday morning.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Japanese dealers think that whether or not to sterilise surplus funds resulting from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is meaningless at a time when the BOJ is already leaving a huge fund surplus in the money market," the dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think the point becomes even less meaningful considering that the fund surplus was expanded to 4.5 trillion yen on Monday due to millennium bug concerns," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A BOJ official said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised the fund surplus to a record level on Monday in order to prevent market concerns about the millennium computer bug from putting upward pressure on the key overnight call rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ increased the surplus to 4.5 trillion yen via its 0020 GMT money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from 2.4 trillion yen on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the BOJ's decision to expand the fund surplus on Monday was viewed strictly as a step to prevent interest rates from rising due to millennium bug concerns, and was not considered a form of credit easing. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473 3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0303GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1998 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   24 Dec.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0128   1.0128   +0.00   -13.59   1.1721\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      102.65   102.89   -0.23    -9.32   113.20\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     104.20   104.19   +0.01   -20.96   131.84\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.5835   1.5857   -0.14   +15.29   1.3735\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.6165   1.6148   +0.11    -2.26   1.6539\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4670   1.4669   +0.01    -4.09   1.5295\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6442   0.6425   +0.26    +5.35   0.6115\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6036   1.6064   -0.17    -0.51   1.6119\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6273   0.6266   +0.11   -10.65   0.7021.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcr07ptj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
