\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen firmer in U.S. as BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fades. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Daniel Sternoff \par \uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 1999\par 16:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Dec 27 (Reuters) - The yen crawled cautiously higher on Monday as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surprise pre-Christmas \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to shake the market's faith that the high-flying yen may have more room to rise. \par \par \uc2  But continued wariness the BOJ may again step into holday-thinned markets and the absence of speculative players in the final trading days of the year kept the yen's gains in check, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In early New York trading, the yen\tab   extended overnight gains from Friday's post-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  low of 103.15 per dollar but stalled around 102.30 yen.\par The Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also pressed to a session high against the euro \tab   as U.S. trading got underway, but its gains were capped above 103.50 yen per euro, nearly 1-1/2 yen below its all-time highs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Most traders stopped dealing this week. Trading is just on a customer basis, mainly Japanese exporters buying yen. I think it will be very difficult for dollar/yen to break out of a 101.50 - 103.50 yen range," said a trader at Sanwa Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the lack of follow-through yen-selling or short-covering after the BOJ's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  confirmed that the yen, lifted by confidence in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economic recovery, has more muscle.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the BOJ was looking to move the yen significantly, they probably could have had quite a bit of success on a thin day like Friday," said Jim McCormick, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at J.P. Morgan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I would interpret as that is obviously not their strategy. They are trying to send the message to the market that 100 yen is a line in the sand," McCormick said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese authorities have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets more than a dozen times since June, voicing concern that yen strength may harm exporters and corporate earnings and derail a fragile economic recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But dealers doubt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be effective.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Next year everybody expects the dollar will go lower again. When market liquidity is larger, the market will try to break the BOJ," said the trader at Sanwa Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par McCormick said a sharp gain in Japan's industrial output for November, which rose by a seasonally adjusted 3.8 percent on the previous month, was further evidence that Japan was indeed emerging from the economic doldrums.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The general tone of the data overnight was upbeat, which makes the Bank of Japan's job that much harder," McCormick aid.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight, the yen did not budge even after the BOJ left a huge 4.5 trillion yen in the Japanese money market, the largest daily surplus ever, as traders did not see this as a signal of an easier monetary policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ itself portrayed the huge surplus as a response to Y2K pressures, as commercial banks coped with heavy customer demand for cash before the year-end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In other trading, the euro\tab   was little changed from its Friday New York close and was locked in very tight ranges in subdued trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro showed negligible reaction to Germany's producer price index for November released early in the European session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par German PPI was up 0.1 percent month-on-month and up 0.7 percent year-on-year, largely in line with expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((-U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1690)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 10:03 a.m. (1503 GMT).  All data\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par daily U.S. close at 4:30 p.m. (2130 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %    1998\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 24 Dec.\tab \tab \tab  Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0130   1.0128   +0.02  -13.57   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     102.29   102.89   -0.58   -9.64   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    103.60   104.19   -0.57  -21.42   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5838   1.5857   -0.12  +15.31   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6158   1.6148   +0.06   -2.30   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4634   1.4669   -0.24   -4.32   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6435   0.6425   +0.16   +5.23   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6052   1.6064   -0.07   -0.42   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6265   0.6266   -0.02  -10.77   0.7021\par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...\tab     Debt...   Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\tab \tab \tab \tab \par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \par \par All spots\tab \par Tokyo spots\t