\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  should  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to curb yen rise - Sakakibara. \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 1999\par 05:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb the yen's rise, Eisuke Sakakibara, a former Finance Ministry official, said on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  "It would be bad if the yen rises above 100 yen to the dollar. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push up the dollar towards 110 yen," he told a TV Asahi programme when asked if the yen's recent rise would have a negative impact on the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trading around 103 yen. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara, former vice-finance minister for international affairs, also said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) should not "sterilise" Friday's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities and criticised the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for sending mixed messages to the markets. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ said it would ease monetary policy, and then later said their policy stance remained unchanged. Those statements have confused the market," he said. \par \par \uc2  Praising the Finance Ministry's decision to conduct dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, Sakakibara said: "The market will be thin towards the end of this year and the beginning of next year, but if needed, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  drastically (in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market)." \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara said the BOJ should conduct so-called "unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", in which the BOJ would not drain excess yen funds stemming from yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and leave them in the money market. \par \par \uc2  "What the BOJ does on Monday and Tuesday would be very important. If the bank says it would not sterilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and ease its monetary policy further, that would stop the yen's rise," he said. \par \par \uc2  ((Yoko Nishikawa, Tokyo Newsroom +81-3-3432-8022 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcq07hk0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
