\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen bruised but not bowed by BOJ action. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 1999\par 14:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 24 (Reuters) - The yen clawed back ground against the dollar on Friday, recovering from lows it hit after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its strength. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was spotted buying dollars from around 102 yen in Asia, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again from around 102.50 yen. Japanese Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda later confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  These sales of yen, which were estimated to have totalled $1-$2 billion, boosted the dollar to a peak of 103.15 yen, up more than one pecent on the day and its highest this week, but by midday in Europe the yen was paring its losses. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the BOJ's main goal had been to slow down the recent yen rise, which could have been amplified by the thin pre-Christmas conditions as several financial centres were already closed. \par \par \uc2  Expectations of further yen strength at the start of 2000 amid renewed interest for Japanese assets, improving economic fundamentals and the beginning of the yearly repatriation for Japanese corporates may have prompted the BOJ into action a day before Christmas, they added. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ is resigned to the fact that the yen is going to get stronger in January but they did not want it to go too far down before the end of the year," said Steven Saywell, market analyst at Fuji in London. \par \par \uc2  "As soon as dollar/yen went down quite sharply to 101.80 the BOJ got very nervous." \par \par \uc2  BOJ'S ACTION SEEN INEFFECTIVE Although wariness of further market action by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should scare off the few yen bulls still around in ultra-thin holiday markets, traders said the inability of the dollar to sustain gains above 103 yen was an indication that the BOJ could not effectively alter market sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Furthermore, no co-ordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected given the proximity with the Christmas break, they added. \par \par \uc2  "The net result (of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is that the market has confirmed that the topside is very heavy," said a dealer at a European bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar may well have stayed above 101 until the yearend even if they did nothing. But now that it seems clear it's not going above 103 anytime soon, selling could accelerate and we might even get below 100 before the year-end." \par \par \uc2  The dollar had shed around half yen its Asian peaks, but was propped above 102.50 in Europe amid BOJ wariness, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese authorities would have hoped to get more bang for their buck in a quiet, pre-Christmas market," said Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  "But it does remind us that the closer you get to 100, the bigger the risks are going to be," he added. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the euro was holding just below 104 yen, after having been boosted nearly one percent to this week's high of 104.56 in the wake of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen strength was keeping the euro propped above $1.01, although the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still below six-day highs around $1.0180 set on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Chartists said the euro had yet to tackle key chart barriers above $1.02 to prove parity was definitely out of the picture. \par \par \uc2  "I would not tell people to get excited about this until we take out levels like $1.0225, $1.0250 or even $1.03," said Steve Wesiak, technical strategist at ABN AMRO in Amsterdam. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in Europe the Bank of Greece surprised the market by cutting by 75 basis points to 11.5 percent its Lombard rate, but left its main 14-day deposit rate unchanged at 10.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  Euro/drachma pushed up toward 331 on the news. \par \par \uc2  Forward rates, derived from interest rate differentials between Greece and the euro zone, edged 10 to 20 basis points lower on the news on speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could soon cut the rest of its rates. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvco07p7q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
