\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen licks its wounds after BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 1999\par 11:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 24 (Reuters) - A bruised yen was struggling to hold ground across the board on Friday, having shed around one percent against the dollar after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its strength in thin, pre-Christmas trading. \par \par \uc2  Top \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Haruhiko Kuroda confirmed on Friday the Bank of Japan bought dollars for yen from around 102 yen in Asia. Tokyo bankers also said they spotted buying from around 102.50 yen and the Japanese Jiji news agency reported the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was estimated to have totalled $1-$2 billion. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the BOJ's main goal had been to stabilise the yen at current levels. No co-ordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected given the proximity with the Christmas break, they added. \par \par \uc2  But wariness of possible further market action by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should scare off the few yen bulls still around in this ultra-thin holiday market, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The yen has been drifting strongly up all week," said Joanne Collins, senior economist at Daiwa Europe in London. \par \par \uc2  "I suppose the BOJ's immediate objective is to send a signal that they are not going to let it break 100 just because it's Christmas." \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR PROPPED AMID BOJ WARINESS \par \par \uc2  The dollar had shed around half yen from a peak of 103.15 yen set in Asia after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but was propped above 102.50 in Europe amid BOJ wariness, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese authorities would have hoped to get more bang for their buck in a quiet, pre-Christmas market," said Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  "But it does remind us that the closer you get to 100, the bigger the risks are going to be," he added. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, offers by Japanese exporters and hedge funds were keeping the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped at around 103. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Friday that Japan must act against speculative moves out of consideration for a quick recovery in the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa said the ministry could feel at ease despite the year-end holiday season. Analysts said Japanese authorities were fearful that the yen's appreciation beyond 100 yen to the dollar would hurt corporate profits and dampen sentiment until a self-sustainable recovery emerges. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the euro was holding around 104 yen EURJPY=), after having been boosted nearly one percent to this week's high of 104.56 in the wake of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen strength was keeping the euro propped above $1.01, although the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still below below six-day highs around $1.0180 set on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Chartists said the euro had yet to tackle key chart barriers above $1.02 to prove parity was definitely out of the picture. \par \par \uc2  "While the euro pushed up yesterday, it is still in a broad consolidating triangle pattern and did not manage to get above $1.0223/35," said Steve Wesiak, technical strategist at ABN AMRO in Amsterdam. \par \par \uc2  "I would not tell people to get excited about this until we take out levels like $1.0225, $1.0250 or even $1.03." \par \par \uc2  The euro derived little support from stronger-than-expected October Italian retail sales, which rose by 3.1 percent year-on-year against expectations for a 2.2 percent rise. This was the largest rise since November, 1998. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvco07oqx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
