\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen forced back by BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 1999\par 09:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 24 (Reuters) - The yen fell across the board, shedding more than one percent against the dollar on Friday, after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength in thin, pre-Christmas trading. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan bought dollars for yen from around 102 yen, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Haruhiko Kuroda confirmed on Friday. Tokyo bankers also said they detected buying later in Tokyo trade on Friday, from around 102.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar gained 1.28 percent on the day to 103.15 yen in Asia, its highest this week, before retreating to around 102.50. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revisited 103 yen in choppy European trade, amid wariness of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Looked at in a micro sense, you would say the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been very successful," said Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese authorities would have hoped to get more bang for their buck in a quiet, pre-Christmas market. But it does remind us that the closer you get to 100, the bigger the risks are going to be," he added. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the dollar needed to rally above 103.85/104.00 yen to scare off yen bulls. There was also a risk of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , either on Friday or next week. \par \par \uc2  "(The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) was a chance for the MOF to show its resolve in stemming sharp yen rises when there is still some liquidity in the market," a dealer at a major Tokyo city bank said. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Friday that Japan must act against speculative moves out of consideration for a quick recovery in the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa said the ministry could feel at ease despite the year-end holiday season. Analysts said Japanese authorities were fearful that the yen's appreciation beyond 100 yen to the dollar would hurt corporate profits and dampen sentiment until a self-sustainable recovery emerges. \par \par \uc2  The euro received a boost against the yen, rising by nearly one percent to a high of 104.36, its strongest this week. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the euro held above $1.01, supported by the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains against the yen but below six-day highs of $1.0180 set on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Italian retail sales rose by 3.1 percent year-on-year in October, the largest rise since November, 1998. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvco07omf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
