\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Christmas spirit sees records tumble. \b0\par\par\uc2 711 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 1999\par 06:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Dec 24 (Reuters) - Hong Kong shares ended at an \par \par \uc2  all-time high on Friday and Tokyo also posted solid gains as a \par \par \uc2  year-end rally on Wall Street gave Asian stock markets a dose \par \par \uc2  of festive cheer. \par \par \uc2      All three major indices on Wall Street hit record levels on \par \par \uc2  Thursday and the underlying tone is still bullish and expected \par \par \uc2  to run over into the new year. \par \par \uc2      Anticipation of a firm start to 2000 is keeping demand for \par \par \uc2  Asian stocks buoyant, although analysts say safe haven plays \par \par \uc2  into markets like Singapore and Hong Kong might be unwound \par \par \uc2  after the turn of the year. \par \par \uc2       SINGAPORE, HANG SENG HIT RECORDS \par \par \uc2      Both the Hang Seng and Straits Times indices hit record \par \par \uc2  levels with the rise on Wall Street and the rally in U.K. \par \par \uc2  stocks keeping investors interested and volume high despite the \par \par \uc2  holiday. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan stocks closed higher for the fourth straight day \par \par \uc2  with a major bank merger helping things along. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan Premier Vincent Siew confirmed on Thursday the \par \par \uc2  mergers of three major state banks in a move aimed at \par \par \uc2  consolidating the island's overcrowded financial industry. \par \par \uc2      Siew was quoted as saying that Bank of Taiwan, the Land \par \par \uc2  Bank of Taiwan and the Central Trust of China - a combination \par \par \uc2  widely tipped by the financial industry - would merge soon. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo stocks were also doing well with a new year rally widely \par \par \uc2  expected if Y2K goes off without a hitch. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  BECALMED \par \par \uc2  The regional \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were becalmed ahead of \par \par \uc2  Christmas, although there was some action on dollar/yen after \par \par \uc2  the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) surprised everyone with a bout of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The BOJ pushed the dollar to a high of 103.10 yen but some \par \par \uc2  sporadic selling from Japanese exporters limited the upside. \par \par \uc2      Traders were wary of pushing the dollar down to 102 where \par \par \uc2  the BOJ stepped in, but they said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely \par \par \uc2  to change bullish sentiment on the yen. \par \par \uc2      Senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Haruhiko \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said earlier Japan will take decisive steps in the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to deal with an excessive rise in the \par \par \uc2  yen. \par \par \uc2  "The current rise in the yen is excessive. An excessive yen \par \par \uc2  rise is not desirable for the Japanese and global economies," \par \par \uc2  he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. $0524 GMT \par \par \uc2  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     102.55\tab  102.29\tab    -0.25\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6680\tab  1.6770\tab    +0.54\par  Taiwan dlr     31.57\tab   31.57\tab    +0.00\par  Korean won   1131.30\tab 1132.00\tab    +0.06\par  Baht\tab      37.55\tab   38.60\tab    +2.80\par  Peso\tab      40.10\tab   40.68\tab    +1.45\par  Rupiah\tab  6980.00\tab 7215.00\tab    +3.37\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \p