\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen hesitates ahead of 4-year peak vs dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 791 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 1999\par 13:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 23 (Reuters) - The yen rose against the dollar and euro on Thursday amid expectations of flows into Japanese assets in 2000, but stopped short of four-year peaks against the dollar and all-time highs against Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Trade was painfully thin, dealers said, due to a market holiday in Japan and the upcoming Christmas break in the U.S. and Europe. \par \par \uc2  But the yen's strength remained intact, and would continue into next year, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "There are good reasons fundamentally for the yen to be strong," said David Coleman, chief economist at CIBC World Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  "The weakness of U.S. bonds has also tended to take the shine off the dollar," he added. \par \par \uc2  Expectations of a Japanese economic recovery have enticed foreign investors into Japanese stocks this year. The Nikkei average rallied by 2.1 percent to close at 18,462 on Wednesday, while U.S. Treasuries closed, in contrast, near two-year lows. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar\tab   was trading around 101.60 yen at 1245 GMT, from the day's low, set in European trade, of 101.33, and from 101.22 reached on November 26, the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakest since December, 1995.\par The euro\tab      edged up to around 102.60 yen from a low on Thursday of 102.12 and an all-time low of 102.03 set on December 6.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But wariness of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  discouraged speculative yen buying for now, analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the Nikkei moves above 19,000, dollar/yen could break 100," said Matthew Clements, economist at Prebon Marshall Yamane in London.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Most people are expecting it to happen at one point, but the general consensus is that a stronger yen would not be tolerated by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , so there might be some form of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BOJ CHRISTMAS MESSAGE?\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might attempt verbal or direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the Christmas and New Year holiday period.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at least a dozen times since June to curb the yen's strength, but has failed to stop an 18 percent rally in the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab   gained a bit of ground against the dollar but remained well within its recent tight range near $1.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reluctance to take fresh positions kept the euro from moving much either way on economic data, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Germany reported that its December preliminary consumer prices rose by 0.2 percent month-on-month and 1.1 percent year-on-year. Average 1999 CPI was up 0.6 percent compared with 1998, the lowest rise since 1991.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro largely ignored a rise in the German DAX stock index to record highs on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par German stocks rose on a government proposal to eliminate the tax on firm-to-firm sales of shareholdings, in a move to boost German industry restructuring. Analysts said the plan, if it becomes law as proposed in 2001, could unleash a wave of mergers and restructuring.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Stephen Hannah, director of research at IBJ International said the tax issue alone was not enough to give the euro a boost.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It depends on the bigger picture in the euro zone. There are other aspects, like their approach to competition, the political scenario in Italy...together with some of these, inflation is picking up relatively fast, so there are quite a few factors to consider."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 1251 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg   YTD %   1998\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   22 Dec\tab \tab \tab   Close\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0092   1.0094   -0.02   -13.90   1.1721\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      101.57   101.68   -0.11   -10.27   113.20\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     102.56   102.53   +0.03   -22.21   131.84\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.5858   1.5855   +0.02   +15.46   1.3735\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.6090   1.6080   +0.06    -2.71   1.6539\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4757   1.4757   +0.00    -3.52   1.5295\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6433   0.6440   -0.11    +5.20   0.6115\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6012   1.6001   +0.07    -0.66   1.6119\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6271   0.6272   -0.02   -10.68   0.7021\par \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...\tab     Debt...   Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \high