\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen sizes up four-year highs vs dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 1999\par 12:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 23 (Reuters) - The yen approached four-year highs against the dollar and all-time highs against the euro on Thursday, buoyed by expectations of flows into Japanese assets in 2000, analysts and dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts could draw little from Thursday's moves, amid a holiday in Japan and thin pre-Christmas trade in Europe. But the trend for a higher yen remained intact, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still looking for excuses to buy the yen, despite the holiday and fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic adviser at Bank of America in London. \par \par \uc2  The dollar JPY=) was trading around 101.60 yen at 1050 GMT, from the day's low, set in European trade, of 101.33, and from 101.22 reached on November 26, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakest since December, 1995. \par \par \uc2  The euro EURJPY=) edged up to around 102.50 yen from a low on Thursday of 102.12 and an all-time low of 102.03 set on December 6. \par \par \uc2  SPECULATORS HOLD BACK \par \par \uc2  Expectations that Japanese equities would continue to look attractive next year contributed to the yen's bullishness, particularly after Wednesday's 2.1-percent rally in the Nikkei average .N225), analysts said. \par \par \uc2  But wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  discouraged speculative yen buying for now, they added. \par \par \uc2  "I think if the Nikkei moves above 19,000, dollar/yen could break 100," said Matthew Clements, economist at Prebon Marshall Yamane in London. \par \par \uc2  "Most people are expecting it to happen at one point, but the general consensus is that a stronger yen would not be tolerated by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so there might be some form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might attempt verbal or direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the Christmas and New Year holiday period. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least a dozen times since June to curb the yen's strength, but has failed to stop an 18 percent rally in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The euro EUR=) gained a bit of ground against the dollar but remained well within its recent tight range near $1.01. \par \par \uc2  Reluctance to take fresh positions kept the euro from moving much either way on economic data, traders said. \par \par \uc2  German preliminary consumer prices rose by 0.2 percent month-on-month and 1.1 percent year-on-year. Average 1999 CPI was up 0.6 percent compared with 1998, the lowest rise since 1991. \par \par \uc2  But analysts continued to predict a rosier future for the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the German DAX stock index rose to record highs on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "You have to have some faith in the fundamentals," said David Coleman, chief economist at CIBC World Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  "We've had more evidence of growth recently, with the strong French industrial production data yesterday and the German Ifo survey last week." \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcn07mu1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
