\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen firm but frustrated as interest dwindles. \b0\par\par\uc2 704 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 1999\par 07:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, Dec 23 (Reuters) - The yen\tab     loitered near\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its session peaks in Thursday afternoon Asian trade, lacking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  the impetus to head higher as trade ground to a virtual \par \par \uc2  standstill. \par \par \uc2      The absence of Tokyo players due to a holiday in Japan \par \par \uc2  hampered liquidity in a market which was already being driven \par \par \uc2  mainly by customer demand amid a dearth of speculative \par \par \uc2  interest. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked well supported, \par \par \uc2  but it was unable to build up the momentum to climb beyond the \par \par \uc2  key 101.20 level against the dollar or revisit its record low \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 102.08 against the euro\tab \tab  reached on December 6.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen briefly notched higher in afternoon trade, but the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise quickly fizzled near the 101.30 level amid a lack of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par follow-through interest and lingering fears of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "No one's doing anything at the moment. It's all on a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par need-to- do basis. No one is doing anything that'll put on a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par risk; they're doing everything to reduce it," said Robert\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Russell, deputy treasurer at Fuji Bank in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But optimism about Japan's economy remained intact and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analysts said expectations of strong inflows to the Nikkei\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par early next year would fuel further gains in the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Year-end dollar sales by Japanese exporters were also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supporting the yen, but dealers said the market was likely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be cautious about pushing it hard in such thin conditions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Right now with few players taking speculative positions,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par if the BOJ were to come in and hit the market hard, it would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par just send the rate soaring," said Marshall Gittler, head of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk group, Asia at Bank of America in Hong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Kong.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "So I don't think people are going to be taking any\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aggressive positions right now," Gittler told Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Fuji's Russell said the market was likely to try and test\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the BOJ's resolve as volumes shrink further into the year-end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He said this could induce the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to show\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its hand and buy both dollars and euros for yen, though he did\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not expect an aggressive move.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I don't think they're going to disturb the market and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par drive it higher... They'd just be making the point that they're\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par out there during the holiday," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The BOJ last \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets on November 30,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying dollars after the yen reached a four-year high of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 101.25.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab     gained a bit of ground but remained well\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par within a tight range, with dealers expecting it to trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between $1.0075 and $1.0120 in the near term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said the yen was attracting what little interest there\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was, and much of this activity was centred on dollar/yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Spreads in the euro/yen\tab \tab  cross had widened out to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as much as 40 ticks, indicating a real reluctance to trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     For full report on major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  click on\tab \par     For previous updates on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves click on\tab \par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0622GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1998 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 22 Dec.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0089   1.0094   -0.05  -13.92   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     101.41   101.68   -0.27  -10.42   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    102.33   102.53   -0.20  -22.38   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5843   1.5855   -0.08  +15.35   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.