\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen powers higher, nears life highs vs euro. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 1999\par 12:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 22 (Reuters) - The yen powered higher on Wednesday toward life highs against the euro and four-year highs against the dollar set in recent weeks, buoyed by strength in Japanese equities. \par \par \uc2  Although U.S. stocks did also gain broadly after the Federal Reserve kept its monetary policy unchanged at its policy meeting on Tuesday, their rises were muted except in the exuberant high-tech sector, from which Tokyo's Nikkei stock price average took cue and soared 2.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  Traders said global capital flows were clearly favouring the yen near term, with the Nikkei wrapping up a banner year which saw foreign investors rushing back in to Japanese equities after a decade of deep sleep. \par \par \uc2  "I think foreign investors' yen asset buying will continue next year, as will Japanese exporters' desperate dollar selling and a slowdown in Japanese investors' foreign investment," said Junpei Yamamoto, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell as low as 101.62 yen, within a half yen of four-year lows near 101.20 set in late November, while the euro dropped to 102.44 yen, approaching life lows near 102 touched in early December. \par \par \uc2  Wariness of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the market jittery, but a Japanese holiday on Thursday was seen reducing the chances of an imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2  In addition, newswire reports of Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa's sanguine comment about the threat of a higher yen to the Japanese economy accelerated the yen's rally in mid-morning Europe. Japan's Jiji Press quoted Miyazawa as saying he had no idea about the dollar's fall below 102 yen. \par \par \uc2  U.S. MARKETS EXPECT EVENTUAL FED TIGHTENING \par \par \uc2  The broader U.S. stock and bond markets were relatively subdued after Tuesday's Federal Open Market Committee meeting, dampening enthusiasm for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The FOMC left interest rates unchanged and maintained a neutral bias but made clear in a statement issued afterwards that it was still concerned about inflationary pressures. \par \par \uc2  "They didn't want to rock the boat before the millennium, but the (Fed's) statement shows that they're obviously still looking to hike rates next year," said Sonja Hellemann, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Paribas Capital Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro was little changed against the dollar, hovering near $1.01 - the middle of a week-long range. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts saw a chance that the euro would stage a rebound after its recent hapless performance due in part to the year-end factors. \par \par \uc2  "I think it will hover around $1.01, but because the market has been so short of euro heading into the year-end, the risk is on the upside," said Will Rugg, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at S&P MMS International in London. \par \par \uc2  Still, so far, the euro has remained steady despite some verbal support from Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet, who said the euro had strong potential to rise. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcm07tgv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
