\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar stays soft vs yen as Nikkei rallies. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 1999\par 09:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 22 (Reuters) - The dollar was soft against the yen on Wednesday after the overnight decision by the U.S. Federal Reserve to keep monetary policy steady provided little support to U.S. asset markets but spurred a rally in Japanese stocks. \par \par \uc2  While perception the Fed was still likely to tighten credit early next year held the Dow Jones Industrial Average and U.S. bond markets in check, Tokyo's Nikkei average rallied 2.11 percent on Wednesday, looking set to wrap up a banner year which saw foreign investors rushing back in to Japanese equities after a decade of deep sleep. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign investors continue to invest heavily in Japanese stocks, and I think that's probably going to help the yen remain relatively strong," said Sonja Hellemann, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Paribas Capital Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  By contrast, analysts noted Wall Street was less exuberant amid lingering U.S. inflation concerns. \par \par \uc2  "They didn't want to rock the boat before the millennium, but the (Fed's) statement shows that they're obviously still looking to hike rates next year," Hellemann said. Concern the yen could continue strengthening in the new year prompted some Japanese exporters to sell dollars, pushing the dollar below 102 yen to within a whisker of Tuesday's three-week lows. A dealer at a Japanese bank in London said wariness of possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the market edgy at sub-102 yen levels. \par \par \uc2  "If you consider what sort of impact \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can have in this thin market, you have to be hesitant," he said. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, a Japanese holiday on Thursday meant there might not be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for at least a few days once BOJ personnel in Tokyo went home, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo, the BOJ released minutes of its policy board meeting held on November 12, and the document revealed one member had expressed concern that a sharp yen rise beyond 105 to the dollar could threaten Japan's recovery. He said a 105-115 yen range would be acceptable for corporations. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also increased the net surplus to 1.5 trillion yen in Japan's money market at its regular \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but officials said the move was aimed at alleviating Y2K funding pressures and did not signal a shift in monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  The euro was little changed against the dollar, hovering near $1.01 - the middle of a week-long range. But its weakness against the yen kept the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally under pressure, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Still, some analysts saw possibilities that the euro would stage a rebound after its recent hapless performance due in part to the year-end factors. \par \par \uc2  "I think it will hover around $1.01, but because the market has been so short of euro heading into the year-end, the risk is on the upside," said Will Rugg, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at S&P MMS International in London. \par \par \uc2  But so far, the euro has remained steady despite some verbal support from Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet, who said the euro had strong potential to rise. \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcm07skv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
