\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro soft in U.S., eyes return to parity. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 709 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 1999\par 16:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Dec 15 (Reuters) - The euro fell to a one-week \par \par \uc2  low on Wednesday, coming within a quarter of a cent of trading \par \par \uc2  at one to one with the dollar again as investors worried about \par \par \uc2  Europe's recovery and cheered America's strong economy. \par \par \uc2  The dollar still benefited from Tuesday's retail sales and \par \par \uc2  consumer price data which showed growth in the U.S. economy \par \par \uc2  remained strong with no signs of inflation. \par \par \uc2  But the euro was little moved by stronger-than-expected \par \par \uc2  German wholesale prices, which rose 3.2 percent in November, \par \par \uc2  marking the biggest increase in more than two years. \par \par \uc2  The euro was off over a quarter of a percent against the \par \par \uc2  dollar at $1.0022 and off about as much against the yen at \par \par \uc2  103.76 yen as New York trading got underway. \par \par \uc2  Dealers predicted more losses for the euro partly because \par \par \uc2  trading volumes were drying up quickly before year end making \par \par \uc2  it easier to push prices around abruptly. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also came close to two-week highs against the \par \par \uc2  yen set on Tuesday, and to 10-year peaks set against the Swiss \par \par \uc2  franc earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  "The market's inclination at the moment is to stick with \par \par \uc2  the trend and for euro/dollar this is down," said Steve Barrow, \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns International in London. \par \par \uc2  "The market is not necessarily moving that much on \par \par \uc2  fundamental news rather it is getting direction from people \par \par \uc2  adjusting their positions." \par \par \uc2  Comments from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief economist Otmar \par \par \uc2  Issing and news that U.S. industrial production rose 0.3 \par \par \uc2  percent in November after rising an adjusted 0.8 percent in \par \par \uc2  October are likely to shape trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The industrial production data, a touch above the market's \par \par \uc2  consensus for a 0.2 percent rise, and capacity utilization at \par \par \uc2  81.0 percent may again reinforce worries of economic \par \par \uc2  overheating again and send U.S. asset markets lower. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday U.S. trade numbers and the Philadelphia Fed \par \par \uc2  survey may offer new reasons to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the euro unwound gains made earlier in the \par \par \uc2  European session on the back of buying by French and German \par \par \uc2  banks. \par \par \uc2  "If Issing fails to say anything supportive for the euro, \par \par \uc2  people will go after the parity level again and if the life low \par \par \uc2  of $0.9985 breaks then it could get very ugly with quick-paced \par \par \uc2  losses toward $0.9850," a dealer at U.S. investment bank said \par \par \uc2  in New York. \par \par \uc2  Earlier the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its refinancing rate \par \par \uc2  steady at 3.0 percent, as expected, following its final \par \par \uc2  policy-setting meeting of the year. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the dollar traded near 103.50 yen, against \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's two-week highs of 103.76, up 2.5 percent from \par \par \uc2  four-year lows set in late November at 101.22. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the yen was undermined by the continued \par \par \uc2  negative undertone to the Nikkei and by the expectation that \par \par \uc2  the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength on \par \par \uc2  further sharp falls in dollar/yen. Dealers said the yen was \par \par \uc2  also suffering a little from recent disappointing Japanese \par \par \uc2  economic data. \par \par \uc2  Sterling, meanwhile, rose briefly against the dollar after \par \par \uc2  British unemployment fell to a 19-year low of 4.1 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1425GMT.  All data taken from \par \par \uc2  Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130GMT. \par \par \uc2  Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1998 \par \par \uc2  Cls \par \par \uc2  14 Dec. \par \par \uc2  ------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0023   1.0057   -0.34  -14.49   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     103.53   103.47   +0.06   -8.54   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    103.74   104.01   -0.26  -21.31   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5955   1.5901   +0.34  +16.16   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6042   1.6110   -0.42   -3.01   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4835   1.4810   +0.17   -3.01   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6350   0.6358   -0.13   +3.84   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.5994   1.5999   -0.03   -0.78   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6249   0.6237   +0.19  -11.00   0.7021\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1607)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcf086q9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
