\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Buoyant dollar puts pressure on euro. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 657 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 1999\par 12:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 15 (Reuters) - The euro eased against the dollar on Wednesday, trading within half a cent of the key one-to-one level as recent evidence of strong but non-inflationary growth in the United States bolstered the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar continued to benefit from Tuesday's retail sales and consumer price data which showed growth in the U.S. economy remained strong with no signs of inflation. In thin trading conditions, the dollar came close to the two-week highs against the yen set on Tuesday, and to the 10-year highs reached against the Swiss franc earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  "The market's inclination at the moment is to stick with the trend and for euro/dollar this is down," said Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns International in London. \par \par \uc2  "The market is not necessarily moving that much on fundamental news and rather getting direction from people adjusting their positions." \par \par \uc2  The euro failed to find any joy in better-than-expected German wholesale prices, which rose 3.2 percent in November, the biggest increase for more than two years. \par \par \uc2  "It seems that we are going to test the life lows again, although parity should provide initial support," said a trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "The whole issue of expanding the European Union and trying to get another lot of countries on board is weighing on the euro heavily." \par \par \uc2  EU heads of state agreed on Saturday to include Turkey and six other countries, mainly from the former Soviet bloc, as formal candidates for entry. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading around $1.0040 at 1034 GMT. Dollar/yen was around 103.50, against Tuesday's two-week highs of 103.76, up 2.5 percent from four-year lows set in late November at 101.22. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the yen was undermined by the continued negative undertone to the Nikkei and by the expectation that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength on further sharp falls in dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yen was also suffering a little from recent disappointing Japanese economic data. Wednesday's figures on industrial production showed a downward revision, while Tokyo area department store sales suffered an un-Christmas-like fall of 4.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  ABSENCE OF GREEK DRAMA \par \par \uc2  The drachma edged higher against the euro in a relief rally after the Bank of Greece cut interest rates by 75 basis points, as expected. \par \par \uc2  The Greek \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its key 14-day deposit rate to 10.75 percent and its Lombard rate to 12.25 percent, saying it believed core inflation and average European Union harmonised inflation rates were headed downwards, despite recent increases in headline inflation. \par \par \uc2  The rate cuts fuelled expectations Greece will revalue the drachma ahead of entering the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The talk all seems to be about a small revaluation and the market is not going to drift too far from where it is currently at on the forwards, until you get actual news on revaluation one way or the other," said Barrow. \par \par \uc2  Greece's updated convergence plan for the 1999-2002 period, released on Wednesday, projected GDP growth picking up to 4.1 percent in 2001 and 4.3 percent in 2002 from 3.8 percent in 2000. The euro was trading just below 330 drachmas at 1049 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Sterling, meanwhile, rose only briefly against the dollar after the British unemployment rate fell to a 19-year low of 4.1 percent. British average earnings in the three months to October rose by a larger-than-expected 4.9 percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was trading a little above earlier one-week lows of $1.6059. The pound eased towards 62.50 pence per euro, from Tuesday's all-time peak around 62.00 pence, amid a positive outlook for the British economy and expectations of higher British interest rates. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcf085d0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
