\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Euro holds slight gains, but seen vulnerable. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 1999\par 22:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Dec 15 (Reuters) - Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose \par \par \uc2  modestly on Wednesday after traders failed to push the euro \par \par \uc2  through the critical one-to-one level with the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell to a one-week low during London trading \par \par \uc2  hours, and New York dealers had braced for fresh losses, \par \par \uc2  betting they would soon probe the euro's life lows at $0.9985. \par \par \uc2  But when liquidity dried up, many dealers were forced to \par \par \uc2  cover short positions even though several said they still \par \par \uc2  believe the euro will head lower in coming days. \par \par \uc2  "There is nothing fundamental driving this move, and it is \par \par \uc2  not taking much to move the market around in these thin \par \par \uc2  conditions," said a dealer at a top European bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar still benefited from Tuesday's retail sales and \par \par \uc2  consumer price data which showed growth in the U.S. economy \par \par \uc2  remained strong with no signs of inflation. \par \par \uc2  Wall Street responded with a 65 point gain on the Dow Jones \par \par \uc2  industrial average. \par \par \uc2  Late in the afternoon, the euro was up 0.13 percent to \par \par \uc2  trade at $1.0070 after it was off over a quarter of a percent \par \par \uc2  against the dollar as New York trading got underway. \par \par \uc2  The euro also swung to a 0.36 percent gain against the yen, \par \par \uc2  erasing its earlier 0.30 percent loss. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also came close to two-week highs against the \par \par \uc2  yen set on Tuesday, and to 10-year peaks set against the Swiss \par \par \uc2  franc earlier this month in overnight trading. \par \par \uc2  "The market's inclination at the moment is to stick with \par \par \uc2  the trend, and for euro/dollar this is down," said Steve \par \par \uc2  Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns International in \par \par \uc2  London. \par \par \uc2  "The market is not necessarily moving that much on \par \par \uc2  fundamental news. Rather, it is getting direction from people \par \par \uc2  adjusting their positions." \par \par \uc2  Traders largely shrugged off a spate of comments from \par \par \uc2  European central bankers and the U.S. Treasury Secretary. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Wim Duisenberg and Bank of \par \par \uc2  France governor Jean Claude Trichet both said the euro has room \par \par \uc2  to rise. \par \par \uc2  Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers, asked about the \par \par \uc2  current weakness of the euro by CNN, gave his standard response \par \par \uc2  about \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We believe that a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in our best interest \par \par \uc2  but it is important in general that countries around the world \par \par \uc2  focus on strengthening their fundamentals," he said. \par \par \uc2  News that U.S. industrial production rose 0.3 percent in \par \par \uc2  November after rising an adjusted 0.8 percent in October failed \par \par \uc2  to directly affect the dollar, but strenghthened the sense that \par \par \uc2  the U.S. economy remains very strong. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday US. trade numbers and the Philadelphia Fed \par \par \uc2  survey may offer new reasons to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  Earlier the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its refinancing rate \par \par \uc2  steady at 3.0 percent, as expected, following its final \par \par \uc2  policy-setting meeting of the year. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the dollar traded at 103.70 yen, against \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's two-week highs of 103.76 yen, up some 2.5 percent \par \par \uc2  from four-year lows set in late November at 101.22. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the yen was undermined by the continued \par \par \uc2  negative undertone to the Nikkei and by the expectation that \par \par \uc2  the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength on \par \par \uc2  further sharp falls in dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yen was also suffering a little from \par \par \uc2  recent disappointing Japanese economic data. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 2100GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1998 \par \par \uc2  Cls \par \par \uc2  14 Dec. \par \par \uc2  ------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0070   1.0057   +0.13  -14.09   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     103.70   103.47   +0.22   -8.39   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    104.38   104.01   +0.36  -20.83   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5886   1.5901   -0.09  +15.66   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6052   1.6110   -0.36   -2.94   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4825   1.4810   +0.10   -3.07   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6357   0.6358   -0.02   +3.96   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.5994   1.5999   -0.03   -0.78   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6267   0.6237   +0.48  -10.74   0.7021\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1607)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcf080f3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pic