\par\par \b \uc2  BIS - Central banks see eurozone growth helping euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 776 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 1999\par 13:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BASLE, Switzerland, Dec 13 (Reuters) - Central bankers attending a regular meeting at the Bank for International Settlements concurred on Monday that euro zone economic growth should help support the euro's exchange rates, Bank of England Governor Eddie George said. \par \par \uc2  "I think the perception was much as it had been before," he told reporters after chairing a meeting of Group of 10 and other central bankers, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels to a substantial degree reflected perceptions of various rates of growth. \par \par \uc2  "I think in particular the expectations about growth in the eurozone accelerating gave reason to hope that the euro would strengthen relative to other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," George said. \par \par \uc2  "I think there is a concern that the yen could prove uncomfortably strong and could actually affect confidence in Japan," he said. But he added, "I think the perception is that the sustained...growth rate in Japan was suggesting that would not happen." \par \par \uc2  Major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been in a state of extreme highs and lows in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  The euro hit a lifetime low below parity to the dollar, and also traded at a lifetime low versus yen earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  Its weakness has also weighed on the Swiss franc, which earlier in December fell to 10-year lows against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The yen recently hit a four-year high against the dollar. The U.S. unit hit its lowest yen levels since December 1995 in late November, with charts showing it as low as 101.22 on November 26. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar when it was near such lows. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami told Japan's parliament last week that Japan would act alone, if necessary, to curb the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with the Wall Street Journal in early December, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Wim Duisenberg said the ECB would never \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone to curb the yen's rise. Duisenberg said he believed the euro's fall was overdone but he wasn't worried by it. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers again last week in Washington reiterated his oft-repeated statement that a strong dollar is in the U.S. national interest. \par \par \uc2  But, speaking to journalists, he declined to comment on recent movements in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The G10 comprises Belgium, Britain, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan, the Netherlands, Sweden, and the United States, as well as Switzerland. ((Zurich newsroom, tel +41 1 631 73 40, fax +41 1 202 55 38, email: zurich.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  "I think in particular the expectations about growth in the eurozone accelerating gave reason to hope that the euro would strengthen relative to other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," George said. \par \par \uc2  "I think there is a concern that the yen could prove uncomfortably strong and could actually affect confidence in Japan," he said. But he added, "I think the perception is that the sustained...growth rate in Japan was suggesting that would not happen." \par \par \uc2  Major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been in a state of extreme highs and lows in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  The euro hit a lifetime low below parity to the dollar, and also traded at a l