\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Ex-MOF Utsumi: Yen Too Strong Given Fundamentals \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui and Shino Kimura \par \uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 1999\par 05:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The Japanese government's official forecast for 0.6% economic growth this fiscal year is too low and probably reflects efforts to create a political environment that would allow the Finance Ministry to step up fiscal spending, a former top official of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday. \par \par \uc2  Keio University professor Makoto Utsumi, formerly vice finance minister for international affairs, said in an interview with Dow Jones Newswires that gross domestic product will likely exceed the official forecast. \par \par \uc2  "The overall trend is positive. I think Japan's GDP should grow more than 1.0% this fiscal year," Utsumi said. \par \par \uc2  "My impression is that the EPA announced an underestimate (for the GDP forecast) to inflate the second extra budget," Utsumi said. \par \par \uc2  Last month, the government unveiled an Y18 trillion spending plan - the second extra budget this year - that came in slightly above market expectations. The Economic Planning Agency has said it may revise the current forecast for 0.6% GDP growth this year, but officials have tried to play down expectations. Earlier Friday, EPA chief Taichi Sakaiya said that forecasts by some private sector economists for 1.0% growth this year are too high. \par \par \uc2  Utsumi warned that the recent strength of the yen against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could hurt Japan's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "This is one potential shadow that could hamper economic growth," Utsumi said. \par \par \uc2  He also said that the current level of the yen against the dollar is too strong, based on current economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  At 0340 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y102.45. \par \par \uc2  "The market is prematurely taking Japan's economic growth into consideration," Utsumi said. \par \par \uc2  Utsumi added that he believes an appropriate range for the dollar would be around Y110. \par \par \uc2  Depending on where \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are, Utsumi added that joint \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps would be useful. \par \par \uc2  For joint \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  cooperation from its G7 partners, however, Utsumi said it might be difficult for them to participate unless certain conditions are met. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already fulfilled its conditions (for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), but for the U.S. and other countries it depends on circumstances," Utsumi said, citing a scenario such as a possible plunge in U.S. stocks and bonds, due to a sharp dollar fall. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether Japan would reaffirm the Group of Seven nations communique issued in September, at the coming G7 meeting scheduled in Tokyo late January, Utsumi said, "I think there is no fundamental change in their perception of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  When asked whether the Bank of Japan was doing enough on the monetary policy front to help ward off yen strength, Utsumi said, "The BOJ is already doing everything it can do." \par \par \uc2  He also said that the BOJ must not turn to underwriting Japanese government bonds in order to cap a possible rise in long-term interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "It's unhealthy for the BOJ to underwrite JGBs," he said, adding that the trend of long-term interest rates should be left up to the market. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The government and politicians are doing too much to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par (bond) market," Utsumi said.\par -By Ron Harui; 813-5255-2942; ron.harui@dowjones.com\par -By Shino Kimura; 813-5255-2929; shino.kimura@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvca08gio\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
