\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Hayami: Will Watch  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Effects On Econ Carefully \b0\par\par\uc2 942 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 1999\par 03:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami said Tuesday that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still can't abandon its zero interest rate policy. \par \par \uc2  "We're not at the stage yet where we can abandon the zero interest rate policy," Hayami said in parliamentary testimony. \par \par \uc2  He said that although the economy has started to show signs of recovering, it still isn't on an autonomous recovery track. \par \par \uc2  Hayami repeated that the BOJ will keep its current zero interest rate policy until deflation fears are gone. \par \par \uc2  He also said that the BOJ will carefully watch moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates to see what kind of impact they have on the economy. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ will continue to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  if \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves become disruptive, Hayami also said. \par \par \uc2  He said if there are disruptive moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will assist the MOF in adjusting the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, as exports have an important role in Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  He also noted that when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  formulates monetary policy, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves should be treated as one important factor. \par \par \uc2  "While it is not appropriate to formulate monetary policy responding only to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, (the BOJ) is always carefully watching the market moves. They are an important factor," Hayami said. \par \par \uc2  Regarding the recent strengthening of the yen, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said, "The yen's rise has been due to hopes for an economic recovery in Japan as well as firm moves in the (Japanese) stock market." \par \par \uc2  He continued, "While the U.S. domestic economy is steadily growing and U.S. stock prices are firm, its current account deficit has worsened." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hayami also said the capital outflow from Japan into the U.S. has been\par decreasing due to fears of a drop in U.S. bond prices and expectations\par of further yen strengthening.\par - - 07/12/99 03-13G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hayami said the BOJ hasn't changed its stance on sterilizing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  funds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  judges overall supply and demand for funds when\par conducting its daily money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and funds that settle\par after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are just one factor that it looks at, Hayami said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen that the BOJ sells to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market during \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par settles after two business days. Some analysts have said that if the BOJ\par didn't drain the funds that settle, it would help ease monetary\par conditions further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ has said such action would make little difference under\par current monetary conditions because there's already a big surplus of\par funds in the market. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also said it will continue to\par watch overall flows of money in deciding how it will conduct its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hayami said that a statement he made on Dec. 1, in which some thought\par he indicated that the bank wouldn't rule out leaving \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  funds unsterilized, was meant to explain the BOJ's\par view to market players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asked whether the BOJ would consider expanding its monthly outright\par buying of government bonds to provide more liquidity, Hayami repeated\par that the BOJ doesn't intend to take such a step because it could lead to\par runaway inflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hayami was speaking in a committee session after submitting the BOJ's\par semi-annual report on the economy and financial markets to parliament.\par -0- 07/12/99 03-47G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the afternoon Diet session, Hayami said the BOJ isn't pessimistic\par over current economic conditions despite Monday's announcement that\par Japan's gross domestic product contracted 1% in the July-September\par quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Even if there's no growth in the October-December and January-March\par periods, (growth in the current fiscal year) will be better than the\par planned figure," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Separately, BOJ Deputy Governor Yutaka Yamaguchi said in the hearings\par that Japanese markets have become less worried about funds drying up\par toward the year-end due to possible Year 2000 (Y2K) problems.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ "has used all of its power to supply funds, and as a result,\par the market is no longer as worried about tight funds," Yamaguchi said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hayami said government bonds to be issued for the second supplementary\par budget can be absorbed by the market and added that he expects calm\par moves in long-term interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "More than Y7 trillion in government bonds are needed for the\par extra-budget. I think the market can absorb (the bonds)," Hayami said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hayami also said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's outright purchases of government\par bills will not lead to further outright purchases of government bonds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I don't think the outright purchase of government bills will be a\par cornerstone for outright purchases of government bonds," Hayami said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He noted that the BOJ decided to extend its outright purchase of\par government bills due to an expected rise in demand for money toward the\par year-end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ's executive director Yoshiharu Obata said in the parliamentary\par testimony that the amount of the BOJ's remaining special loans to\par financial institutions was Y876.5 billion as of November 6, which\par included Y329.9 billion for the failed Yamaichi Securities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He added that the BOJ provided the financial assistance to financial\par institutions only if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  judged that the borrowers are\par capable of returning those funds to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The BOJ's assistance is just temporary," Obata said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par When asked about harsh criticism from former vice finance minister for\par international affairs Eisuke Sakakibara Monday that the BOJ governor\par should resign if he cannot be cautious in making comments, Hayami said:\par "I took (Sakakibara's remarks) as encouragement under the guise of a\par reprimand."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvc708b27\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
