\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro attempts frail recovery vs rampant yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 746 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 1999\par 09:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 6 (Reuters) - The euro inched up from life lows against a broadly strong yen and backtracked against the dollar on Monday, but analysts said that it would struggle to extend its rebound in the absence of fresh euro zone economic reports. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Monday the yen had shrugged off weaker-than-expected third quarter Japanese gross domestic product data and staged a broad rally as traders chose to focus instead on an upward revision to the second quarter figures. \par \par \uc2  Remarks by Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was pursuing a strong euro policy helped the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to climb back from life lows against the yen and from day's lows around $0.9995. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said that without new data and in the absence of statements showing ECB officials were worried enough about the euro's weakness to act, the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risked falling to new lows. \par \par \uc2  "There's not a great deal to change the positive sentiment on the yen in the medium term," said Audrey Childe-Freeman, economist at CIBC World Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  "As far as Europe is concerned Trichet's comments gave nothing to the market to get excited about. He did not suggest anything to make the market worried about potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from European authorities. The euro will remain in a narrow range but for choice will continue to develop this weak bias." \par \par \uc2  The euro was within a quarter yen of its all-time lows around 102.10 yen and its weakness was preventing euro/dollar from rising decisively above parity. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the charts suggested the euro was set to fall gradually against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The move down will be quite slow, but it looks like a one-way street," said Stuart Frost, market strategist at NatWest GFM in London, who expects euro/yen to go to 100. \par \par \uc2  MARKET BELIEVES JAPAN'S RECOVERY STORY \par \par \uc2  The yen was initially dented after Japanese GDP data showed a 1.0 percent fall in the July to September quarter against market forecasts of a more modest 0.2 percent dip. \par \par \uc2  But the news did not look nearly as grim when the Economic Planning Agency announced it was revising up second quarter growth to 1.0 percent from just 0.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the reaction to Japan's GDP data illustrated how investor sentiment was stacked up in favour of Japan and against Europe at the moment. \par \par \uc2  "The market believes in the Japanese recovery story and ignores anything to the contrary," said a European bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "But no matter how good euro data is, no one wants to listen. It's a mindset that'll take time to change." \par \par \uc2  He noted that GDP data from the European Union and Germany this week were expected to show reasonable growth, but all the talk in markets was of how the authorities had abandoned the euro and were interfering with corporate restructuring. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors were especially upset with German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder who on Sunday declared that markets were sometimes wrong and needed corrective government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In contrast, analysts seemed prepared to forgive \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  anything with most putting a positive spin on the GDP data. \par \par \uc2  "Essentially, we believe these figures understate the strength of the economy," said James Malcolm, an economist at J.P.Morgan in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "If you look at the production side of the economy it's doing very well, but that's simply not captured in these figures," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0837GMT.  All data taken from \par \par \uc2  Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130GMT. \par \par \uc2  Last     US Close  % Chg   YTD %   1998 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 03 Dec.\tab \tab \tab  Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0022   1.0022   +0.00   -14.50   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab      102.11   102.67   -0.55   -14.50   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab     102.35   102.90   -0.53    -9.80   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.5912   1.5909   +0.02   +15.85   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.6006   1.6000   +0.04    -3.22   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4790   1.4793   -0.02    -3.30   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6317   0.6319   -0.03    +3.30   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.5956   1.5946   +0.06    -1.01   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6257   0.6257   +0.00   -10.88   0.7021\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc608l15\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
