\par\par \b \uc2  Hayami - Unsterilised  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk meaningless. \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1999\par 08:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 3 (Reuters) - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaru Hayami told parliament on Friday the BOJ is supplying ample funds to the money market but that it regards as meaningless a debate about whether it should leave the yen proceeds of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, making the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  "unsterilised". \par \par \uc2  Ansering questions in the Lower House Finance Committee, Hayami reiterated that the BOJ intends using its regular money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave enough money in the market to keep short-term rates essentially at zero. \par \par \uc2  This would include the yen generated from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said, but added: "Within the context of the zero interest rate policy, the debate about whether to sterilise or unsterilise is meaningless." \par \par \uc2  Since May, the BOJ has left a daily surplus of about one trillion yen in the short-term money market to keep rates at zero, and the BOJ argues that this amount swamps the amount that must be settled from any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Proponents of unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  say it would augment the effect of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value through oversupply. \par \par \uc2  But the BOJ also says that increasing the one trillion yen "idle balance" in the market would merely put more money in the hands of "tanshi" short-term money brokers and would have no effect on the economy. \par \par \uc2  Hayami said a statement he issued on Wednesday - which prompted reports by some in the media that the BOJ had shifted to unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - was aimed at restating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unchanged intent to provide ample funds to the market. \par \par \uc2  The bank issued the statement, which expressed support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , just after the BOJ sterilised Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , keeping the trillion yen surplus intact. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did the same on Thursday, which was the settlement day for tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ((William Mallard, Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432-8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc308wj3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
