\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Japan, ECB douse hopes of G7 action on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By William Mallard \par \uc2 642 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1999\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 3 (Reuters) - Japan and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday quashed any lingering expectations that the world's top three central banks would cooperate to boost the wilting euro and curb the rampant yen. The Bank of Japan, which fought a lone battle this week in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to hold back the yen by buying dollars and euros, conceded it would be difficult for the United States to join in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  And the ECB chief, Wim Duisenberg, strongly reinforced market perceptions that the bank is unconcerned about the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which slid on Friday below $1.00 for the first time. \par \par \uc2  Central banks are known for acting when least expected, but Friday's public comments offered no hints of looming concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Group of Seven leading industrial powers. \par \par \uc2  U.S. SEEN UNLIKELY TO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , DUISENBERG INDIFFERENT \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami told parliament that the strong U.S. economy, with its appetite for imports, has caused the nation's current account deficit to balloon to some four percent of gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  "In such a situation, I think it would be difficult for the U.S. to join a yen-selling, dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Hayami said. \par \par \uc2  Appearing in the same Lower House committee, Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa reiterated that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen spiked higher but also held out little hope that the rest of the Group of Seven would join in. \par \par \uc2  "It is not so easy to agree and coordinate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is not so large it is unavoidable that we will take the responsibility to act." \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa said he thought the European authorities were not very worried about the decline in the euro, which is down some 16 percent against the dollar since its January launch and 24 percent against the yen. \par \par \uc2  ECB president Wim Duisenberg confirmed Miyazawa's hunch, telling the Wall Street Journal that even though he thought the euro's drop overdone, he was not worried about it. \par \par \uc2  He said the euro's weakness was not increasing the risk of inflation in the 11-country euro-zone and the yen's strength was not posing a danger to the global economy. \par \par \uc2  Asked if there were circumstances under which the ECB would join \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, Duisenberg said: "No, never with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone. There are circumstances where there could be coordinated action between the three big central banks, but I don't foresee that at this time." \par \par \uc2  JAPAN ON ITS OWN FRETTING ABOUT STRONG YEN \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg's comments contrast with those of Japanese officials, who have repeatedly said a September G7 statement - that the rest of the group shares Japan's concern about the rising yen's impact on the global economy - was still in force. \par \par \uc2  Although Japanese sales of yen on Monday and Tuesday braked the dollar's fall before it could slide below 100 yen, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders remain keen to snap up the yen and dump the euro. \par \par \uc2  The yen is near four-year highs against the dollar as global investors have bought Japanese assets on growing signs of an economic recovery, while exports to Asia have remained firm. \par \par \uc2  Many economists and even some officials say Japan is becoming more resilient to a strong yen, even though it makes life harder for exporters, increases deflationary pressure on the economy and erodes the yen value of Japanese firms' overseas earnings. \par \par \uc2  The next check on the economy's health will come on Monday when the government releases gross national product data. \par \par \uc2  Economists expect the economy shrank a little in the July-September period after surprisingly strong growth in the first half of the year. ((Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432-8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc308vtt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
