\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Treasuries weaker in Tokyo before jobs data. \b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1999\par 09:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 3 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasuries were weaker in late afternoon trading on Friday, following overnight selloffs triggered by record U.S. home sales in October. \par \par \uc2  Wariness that more U.S. rate hikes may be on the horizon kept Japanese investors at bay ahead of the release later on Friday of the keenly awaited U.S. jobs report for November. \par \par \uc2  Given the recent rise of the yen against the dollar, partly reflecting increased foreign investment in Japan, Japanese investors are largely holding back from building fresh positions in the U.S. Treasuries market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 30-year Treasury bond was at 97-10/32 as of 0730 GMT, yielding 6.32 percent, down from 97-13/32 in New York late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Investors are deadly quiet," said a senior dealer at a major Japanese brokerage house. \par \par \uc2  He said it seemed as if the authorities, in an attempt to prevent money from flooding overseas, are content with the yen's rising trend as long as it is gradual. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Monday and Tuesday to smoothe out disruptive market moves. Since then, the dollar has been relatively steady around 102.50 yen, off a four-year low of 101.25 yen touched on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Economists surveyed by Reuters forecast, on average, that November nonfarm payrolls likely grew by 226,000 jobs after October's 310,000 increase. \par \par \uc2  The hourly wage rate probably rose 0.3 percent, with the jobless rate seen unchanged at 4.1 percent, the lowest level in three decades. The payroll figures are due at 1330 GMT. \par \par \uc2  .. \par \par \uc2   for Key U.S. Treasury Rates \par \par \uc2   for USD GovPX-UST-Curve \par \par \uc2   for day's worldwide U.S. bond reports \par \par \uc2   for day's Tokyo U.S. bond reports. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc308uzi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
