\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro hovers above dlr parity, awaits Europe. \b0\par\par\uc2 914 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1999\par 08:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 3 (Reuters) - The euro hovered slightly above parity with the dollar in subdued late Asian trade on Friday as players waited for their European counterparts to join in and map out a direction for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro was the centre of attention during most of the Tokyo trading day, dropping in the morning to match a lifetime low hit overnight at $0.9995, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "It's most likely that the euro will test parity again during European hours after doing so in New York and Tokyo, and then the market will want to see how far it goes," said a Japanese city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  At 0600 GMT, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at $1.0007/17 compared with $1.0008 in late New York trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said it appeared the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) was not as concerned as the market about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling below $1.00. \par \par \uc2  "Their main concern at this moment seems to be how to curb inflation, while the level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is secondary. They aren't quick to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market like Japanese authorities," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  In an interview published by the Wall Street Journal on Friday, ECB President Wim Duisenberg was quoted as saying that the euro's weakness was not increasing the risk of euro-zone inflation. \par \par \uc2  He said he thought the euro's fall was overdone but that he was not concerned about it, and that the only significance of the euro falling to parity at $1.00 was psychological. \par \par \uc2  Although stop-loss offers were seen building up around $0.9990 and speculators were seen aiming for rumoured options positions at $0.9950, dealers said they were also focused on the effect U.S. jobs data to be released on Friday would have on the market. \par \par \uc2  According to a consensus of economists polled by Reuters, nonfarm payrolls, to be released at 1330 GMT, are expected to have risen 226,000 in November after a 310,000 gain in October. \par \par \uc2  The dollar may strengthen against the euro if the figure is larger than forecast due to bearish sentiment looming over the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo, the euro was supported mainly by short-covering as well as options-related bids. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the greenback could weaken against the yen as strong numbers would mean the U.S. economy is overheated, triggering renewed fears of inflation and undermining the stock market and hurting the dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Friday, the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded in a narrow range against the yen - between around 102.40 and 102.80 yen\tab   - with selling orders by Japanese exporters and foreign players near 103 yen and support just under 102 yen on wariness over possible Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After two consecutive days of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action on Monday and Tuesday, traders said the support level for the dollar has inched higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The resistance level is stuck at around 102.80, but the downside has gradually inched up. From around 101.50, it came up to 102.00 and today the support has been above 102 yen," another city bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar stood at 102.36/46 yen\tab   by 0659 GMT from 102.74 in late New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One factor maintaining the dollar's strength on Friday was the expectation that Japan's third-quarter gross domestic product figures could be weaker than previously thought, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economic Planning Agency chief Taichi Sakaiya said earlier in the day that Japan may post an economic contraction for the July-September quarter in the data due out on Monday, due to low public investment and capital spending.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After surprise GDP growth in the first two quarters of the year, a Reuters poll on Thursday found economists expected a slight decline in July-September, with the median forecast at a 0.2 percent quarter-on-quarter decline. In their previous forecast they saw flat growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar edged lower against the yen in afternoon trade after BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami told parliament that other nations including Asia were not very worried about the yen's appreciation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hayami also said he though a yen-selling, dollar-buying joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was difficult for the United States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also strengthened against the euro as Japanese institutions caught up with the overnight action. The euro slipped to 102.52/62 yen\tab      from 102.84 in late New York on Thursday. ((Ayumi Moriyama, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8550 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0706 GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last  US Close  % Chg   YTD %   1998 Close\par \tab \tab \tab \tab      02 Dec.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0002   1.0008   -0.06   -14.67   1.1721\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      102.37   102.74   -0.36   -14.67   113.20\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     102.45   102.84   -0.38    -9.57   131.84\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.5966   1.5965   +0.01   +16.24   1.3735\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5978   1.5994   -0.10    -3.39   1.6539\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4810   1.4815   -0.03    -3.17   1.5295\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6328   0.6326   +0.03    +3.48   0.6115\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.5986   1.5989   -0.02    -0.83   1.6119\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6254   0.6255   -0.02   -10.92   0.7021.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc308uuf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
