\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro circling parity with gains seen elusive. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1999\par 09:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 3 (Reuters) - The euro was circling $1.00 on Friday after falling to all time lows below there in Asian trading and was not expected to make a significant recovery in the near term. \par \par \uc2  However looking ahead to the new year, analysts said the economic backdrop in Europe would support an appreciation of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Most likely we will test parity a couple more times and probably go towards $0.99/0.98," said Michael Rottmann, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist HypoVereinsbank, Munich. \par \par \uc2  "December is a somewhat critical month for the euro. We will probably see some window-dressing towards the end of the month as no one will want to go into the new year with too much euro exposure given its underperformance so far this year." \par \par \uc2  In January he said there was a chance of improving sentiment towards the euro because economic data favoured somewhat higher levels for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro is currently hovering just above $1.00 after finally cracking one-to-one parity against the dollar in U.S. trading on Thursday, and falling to an all time low around $0.9990 in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said comments from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg on Thursday that the German government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rescue construction company Philipp Holzmann Ag did not enhance Europe's image were helping to undermine confidence in the euro. \par \par \uc2  "Chancellor Schroeder's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (to rescue Holzmann) has not helped but he is not responsible," said David Bloom, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at HSBC Markets. \par \par \uc2  He said trading conditions were driving the market with the bounce in U.S. asset markets in part a cause of the euro's decline, coupled with investor selling of euro/yen. \par \par \uc2  "In thin markets, this group of investors are having a disproportionate impact on the market," said Bloom. \par \par \uc2  "While the euro is under two-pronged attack, the omens are not good. I would say, do not fight it." \par \par \uc2  For Friday, analysts said the market focus would be on the U.S. November non-farm payrolls report at 1330 GMT. \par \par \uc2  According to a consensus of economists polled by Reuters, nonfarm payrolls are expected to have risen 226,000 in November after a 310,000 gain in October. \par \par \uc2  The dollar may strengthen against the euro if the figure is larger than forecast due to bearish sentiment looming over the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR/YEN TRADING SIDEWAYS FOR NOW \par \par \uc2  The yen traded in a narrow range against the dollar - between around 102.20 and 102.80 - with selling orders by Japanese exporters and foreign players near 103 yen and support just under 102 yen on wariness over possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  After two consecutive days of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Monday and Tuesday, traders said the support level for the dollar had inched higher. \par \par \uc2  "The resistance level is stuck at around 102.80, but the downside has gradually inched up. From around 101.50, it came up to 102.00 and today the support has been above 102 yen," said a city bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  One factor helping maintain dollar/yen's strength on Friday was the expectation that Japan's third-quarter gross domestic product figures could be weaker than previously thought. \par \par \uc2  Economic Planning Agency chief Taichi Sakaiya said earlier in the day that Japan may post an economic contraction for the July-September quarter in the data due out on Monday, due to low public investment and capital spending. \par \par \uc2  After surprise GDP growth in the first two quarters of the year, a Reuters poll on Thursday found economists expected a slight decline in July-September, with the median forecast at a 0.2 percent quarter-on-quarter decline. In their previous forecast they saw flat growth. \par \par \uc2  "If the GDP is slightly below zero dollar/yen should stay stable at around current levels, but combined with a somewhat weaker euro/dollar exchange rate we could see a test of the 100 level in euro/yen," said Hypovereinsbank's Rottmann. The dollar edged lower against the yen in afternoon trade after BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami told parliament that other nations including Asia were not very worried about the yen's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Hayami also said he though a yen-selling, dollar-buying joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was difficult for the United States. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc308pv4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
