\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Frail euro tiptoes away from dollar parity. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 826 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1999\par 12:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 3 (Reuters) - The euro regained a toehold above lifetime lows it fell to against the dollar on Friday, inching away from the crucial on-to-one level it breached a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the euro was still at risk of dropping back through parity against the dollar and predicted this level to be breached again soon. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that bears may try to push the euro down again any time since remarks made by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisemberg to the Wall Street Journal on Friday suggested the bank was not concerned about its slide through $1.0. \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg told the U.S. paper that the break was only of psychological significance. He added that the ECB would never act with Japan alone to weaken the yen and that he did not foresee coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ECB and the Federal Reserve for the time being. \par \par \uc2  "The euro is still vulnerable to further losses, particularly as the latest comments by Duisenberg seem to suggest the ECB is not keen to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment," said Patrick O'Sullivan, economist at AIB Group Treasury in Dublin. \par \par \uc2  "The key today would be U.S. payrolls. If they come in below expectations this could underpin the U.S. stock market, support the dollar, and we could see euro/dollar falling back through parity." \par \par \uc2  The euro is currently hovering around $1.0030 after falling to an all-time low around $0.9990 in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. November non-farm payrolls report was due out at 1330 GMT. According to a consensus of economists polled by Reuters, nonfarm payrolls are expected to have risen 226,000 in November after a 310,000 gain in October. \par \par \uc2  ECB's council member Klaus Liebscher said on Friday that the euro weakness was exacerbated bu the thin year-end volumes. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Duisenberg's comments on Thursday that the German government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rescue construction company Philipp Holzmann Ag did not enhance Europe's image were also helping to undermine confidence in the euro. \par \par \uc2  "Chancellor Schroeder's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (to rescue Holzmann) has not helped but he is not responsible," said David Bloom, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at HSBC Markets. \par \par \uc2  EURO'S FUTURE BRIGHTER INTO NEW YEAR \par \par \uc2  However, looking ahead to the new year, analysts said the economic backdrop in Europe would support an appreciation of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the new year. \par \par \uc2  "December is a somewhat critical month for the euro," said Michael Rottmann, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HypoVereinsbank in Munich. "We will probably see some window-dressing towards the end of the month as no one will want to go into the new year with too much euro exposure given its underperformance so far this year." \par \par \uc2  He said there was a chance of improving sentiment towards the euro in January given the improved economic background. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the yen traded in a narrow range against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The resistance level is stuck at around 102.80, but the downside has gradually inched up. From around 101.50, it came up to 102.00 and today the support has been above 102 yen," said a city bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  One factor helping maintain dollar/yen's strength on Friday was the expectation that Japan's third-quarter gross domestic product figures could be weaker than previously thought. \par \par \uc2  Economic Planning Agency chief Taichi Sakaiya said earlier in the day that Japan may post an economic contraction for the July-September quarter in the data due out on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "If the GDP is slightly below zero, dollar/yen should stay stable at around current levels, but combined with a somewhat weaker euro/dollar exchange rate we could see a test of the 100 level in euro/yen," said Hypovereinsbank's Rottmann. \par \par \uc2  The dollar edged lower against the yen in earlier trade after BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami told parliament that other nations including Asia were not very worried about the yen's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  ((Lisa Jucca, London Capital Markets 0171 542 6745)). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1104GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at \par \par \uc2  2130GMT. \par \par \uc2  Last    US Close  % Chg   YTD %   1998 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 02 Dec.\tab \tab \tab Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0024   1.0008   +0.16   -14.48   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab      102.40   102.74   -0.33   -14.48   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab     102.66   102.84   -0.18    -9.54   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.5943   1.5965   -0.14   +16.08   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5996   1.5994   +0.01    -3.28   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4808   1.4815   -0.05    -3.18   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6311   0.6326   -0.24    +3.21   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.5988   1.5989   -0.01    -0.81   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6262   0.6255   +0.11   -10.81   0.7021\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908d