\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ leaves market surplus, sterilising  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1999\par 01:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it left the money market with a projected net surplus of 1.0 trillion yen on Thursday, effectively sterilising its yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The surplus amount was unchanged from the level left after the BOJ's Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In its regular 0020 GMT money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to sell 600 billion yen worth of bills through an auction, effectively absorbing the excess funds it created through its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales on Tuesday. As a result, the net projected surplus in the money market on Thursday was 1.0 trillion yen, the BOJ said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the BOJ's stance to leave the net surplus in the money market unchanged from Wednesday indicates that it sterilised - or drained excess yen funds created by - the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it had conducted on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Izumi Yamashita, director of the BOJ's financial markets department, quashed speculation of a further monetary easing by the BOJ, saying the whole argument of whether or not to sterilise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "meaningless" under the BOJ's zero interest rate policy. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ, acting as the government's agent, repeatedly sold yen on Tuesday to buy dollars and euros, lifting the dollar as high as 103.10 yen from a low of 101.35 yen. \par \par \uc2  Settlements on the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday will occur on Thursday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473-3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc2091ot\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
