\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro sets life low just above parity vs dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1999\par 09:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The euro set all-time lows perilously close to one-for-one with the dollar on Thursday, while the equally psychological 100 yen barrier remained in sight for both euro and dollar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said concerns about liquidity in the run-up to the millennium were driving investors away from the euro and towards U.S. assets, the world's most liquid market. \par \par \uc2  The euro's latest fall against the dollar comes after the U.S. Dow Jones Industrial Average rallied by more than one percent on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The perception in the financial markets that European policymakers are not concerned by the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall has also weighed on the euro. Traders are now focusing on the news conference the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to hold after its fortnightly meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "It seems likely that we will test parity, it's just a matter of time," said David Brickman, international economist at PaineWebber in London. \par \par \uc2  "The next key event is the ECB press conference, and every time European central bankers or finance ministers open their mouths, the euro goes down." \par \par \uc2  The euro fell to a low of $1.0023, a fall of nearly 15 percent from its launch rate in January, before recovering by 1/3 of a cent to trade just over $1.0050 at 0830 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the release on Friday of U.S. employment data could also have a negative impact on the euro. \par \par \uc2  November non-farm payrolls are forecast to rise by 226,000, from a previous gain of 310,000. \par \par \uc2  "If the payrolls are particularly strong, that could also do the damage for the euro," Brickman said. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo traders reported talk that more options positions at $1.0000 and $0.9950 were expiring in New York on Thursday and once they were out of the way, the banks defending them would presumably withdraw their bids, so opening the way for a test of parity. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the longer-term outlook for the euro remained favourable, with growth in the euro zone likely to outstrip the U.S. in 2000. \par \par \uc2  French consumer confidence jumped to a record of +1 in November, from -3 in October, data released on Thursday showed. \par \par \uc2  YEN DEALERS WARY OF BOJ \par \par \uc2  The yen, meanwhile, traded in narrow ranges around 102.50 to the dollar and 103 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan (BOJ) kept its daily money market surplus at one trillion yen on Thursday, confounding speculation that it would leave Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised. \par \par \uc2  "People have stopped dealing by now ahead of key U.S. jobs data due tomorrow," said one Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Also, we are showing respect to the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities as they did what they had warned," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has confirmed that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to rein in the yen's rise on Monday and Tuesday after two months' absence. \par \par \uc2  Since then, there has been no trace in the market of the BOJ, which acts as agent for the ministry in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bankers said. \par \par \uc2  They said it is difficult to assess the amount of the BOJ's yen selling for the two days as thin activity may have exaggerated the magnitude of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but many estimated that yen selling for the dollar and euro by the BOJ totalled the equivalent of around $5 billion. \par \par \uc2  The estimate was relatively small compared with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the summer, but verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said the yen's rise was still excessive and that the ministry would take decisive action on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed. \par \par \uc2  "The yen is too strong against the dollar and the euro. The euro is too weak against the yen and the dollar," he added. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc2090jc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
