\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen firm vs dlr and euro, capped by BOJ fear. \b0\par\par\uc2 946 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1999\par 08:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The yen was a tad firmer against the dollar and euro by late Tokyo trade on Thursday but failed to hold on to earlier gains amid wariness over potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities. \par \par \uc2  The yen had risen by midday after the Bank of Japan (BOJ) kept its daily money market surplus at a trillion yen, confounding speculation that it would leave Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's decision drove home the message given by BOJ officials on Wednesday when they dismissed talk of not sterilising, saying the issue was irrelevant. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ officials said the current zero interest rate policy was a more effective way of supplying liquidity to the money market than so-called unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the yen soon stopped rising at 102.35 to the dollar and 103 to the euro amid lack of aggressive buyers, before activity waned by late afternoon. \par \par \uc2  "People have stopped dealing by now ahead of key U.S. jobs data due tomorrow," said one Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Also, we are showing respect to the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities as they did what they had warned," he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As of 0624 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 102.50/60 yen\tab   against 102.69 yen in late U.S. trading on Wednesday.\par The euro was at 103.30/39 yen\tab      against 103.53 yen in late U.S. trading on Wednesday.\par Against the dollar, the euro was at $1.0069/76\tab  , little changed from $1.0076 in late U.S. trading on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders reported talk that more options positions at $1.0000 and $0.9950 were expiring in New York on Thursday and once they were out of the way the banks defending them would presumably withdraw their bids, so opening the way for a test of parity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Major support was seen at $1.0036, the lifetime low from Monday, and parity was obviously a big psychological level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Apart from wariness over BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the dollar was well-supported by bids below 102 yen by Japanese investors covering short positions taken earlier for hedging purposes and bids by overseas operators.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Buybacks by short-term traders locking in profits propped up the euro after Japanese institutional investors dumped it for yen by midday, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has confirmed that it \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to rein in the yen's rise on Monday and Tuesday after two months absence.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Since then, there has been no trace in the market of the BOJ, which acts as agent for the ministry in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , bankers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said it is difficult to assess the amount of the BOJ's yen selling for the two days as thin activity may have exaggerated the magnitude of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but many estimated that yen selling for the dollar and euro by the BOJ totalled the equivalent of around $5 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The estimate was relatively small compared with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's massive yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during the summer, but verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said on Thursday the yen's rise was still excessive and that the ministry would take decisive action on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if needed.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The yen is too strong against the dollar and the euro. The euro is too weak against the yen and the dollar," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Kuroda's comments seemed in line with private economists' view over the current conditions of the Japanese economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Reuters poll of economists released on Thursday showed they are slightly less optimistic about how the Japanese economy fared in the July-September quarter than they were a month ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Recent signs of weaker consumption are the main reason behind the downward revisions, economists say, with the latest survey resulting in a median forecast of a 0.2 percent decline quarter-on-quarter in July-September GDP compared with the forecast last month, which saw flat growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Economic Planning Agency (EPA) will release GDP data on Monday at 8:50 a.m. (2350 GMT Sunday).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We don't dare take action from the current levels in either dollar/yen or euro/yen," said one U.S. bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said there was caution about chances that European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board members may try to talk up the euro's prospects at a post-meeting news conference later on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Officials have been arguing that the euro's fundamentals are positive but marred the message by expressing a lack of concern at its weakness. That gave speculators the impression there was little risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if they pushed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower. ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0725 GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1998 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   01 Dec.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0062   1.0076   -0.14   -14.15   1.1721\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      102.48   102.69   -0.20    -9.47   113.20\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     103.08   103.53   -0.43   -21.81   131.84\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.5900   1.5879   +0.13   +15.76   1.3735\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.6008   1.6002   +0.04    -3.21   1.6539\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4743   1.4727   +0.11    -3.61   1.5295\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6344   0.6364   -0.31    +3.74   0.6115\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6005   1.6011   -0.04    -0.71   1.6119\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6279   0.6302   -0.36   -10.57   0.7021.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc2090ef\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
