\par\par \b \uc2  SNB rumours swirl around  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mkt, denied by cenbank. \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1999\par 12:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The Swiss National Bank on Thursday became the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  name to be bandied around by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers on the lookout for unusual activity on the foreign exchanges. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied it made a foray into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  But the sensitivity of prices to even a hint of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  highlighted concern that monetary officials may be keen to send a protest to the market, either overtly or covertly, about recent extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. \par \par \uc2  The past week has seen the yen surge across the board, the euro hit lifetime lows against the dollar and the yen, and the dollar rally to its highest this decade against the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  Traders said speculation the SNB had been buying Swiss francs for dollars surfaced earlier in Europe after the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened towards Monday's decade-long trough of 1.5975 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  But the SNB told Reuters: "We have not been active in the market." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar had settled at around 1.5850 Swiss francs\tab   by 1048 GMT, down 0.7 percent from the day's peaks.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers have been on alert for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold yen for other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday and again on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  followed the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's surge to four-year highs against the dollar on Friday and its rally to all-time peaks against the euro this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wariness was also rife that the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could step in to halt a slide which took Europe's 11-month old single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to within a quarter cent of the psychological one-for-one rate against the dollar on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Right at the beginning of the (European) session there was talk the SNB was selling dollar/Swiss and more recently there were worries about the ECB checking rates," said a trader at a European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Swaha Pattanaik, London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc208x9e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
