\par\par \b \uc2  Chronology of key milestones in euro's first year. \b0\par\par\uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1999\par 23:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Dec 2 (Reuters) - Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell below one U.S. dollar for the first time on Thursday, down almost 15 percent since its launch at the start of 1999. \par \par \uc2  Following is a chronology of key milestones in the fall of the euro against the dollar since January 1: \par \par \uc2  * JANUARY 1, 1999 - Euro officially launched by Austria, Belgium, Finland, France, Germany, Ireland, Italy, Luxembourg, Netherlands, Portugal, Spain \par \par \uc2  * JANUARY 4 - Euro starts trading at $1.1747 in Sydney \par \par \uc2  * JANUARY 29 - Data show U.S. economy grew 5.6 percent in fourth quarter of 1998. Euro closes in New York at $1.1363 \par \par \uc2  * FEBRUARY 22 - Euro sets life low after finance ministers from Group of Seven industrialised countries say \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should reflect economic fundamentals. Euro closes at $1.1035 \par \par \uc2  * MARCH 15 - European Commission resigns en-masse. Euro closes at $1.0943 \par \par \uc2  * MARCH 16 - Dow Jones industrial average of leading U.S. stocks hits 10,000 for first time. Euro closes at $1.0990 \par \par \uc2  * MARCH 24 - NATO attacks Yugoslavia. Euro at $1.0885 \par \par \uc2  * APRIL 8 - ECB cuts its key market interest rate by a half-percentage point to 2.5 percent. Euro closes at $1.0761 \par \par \uc2  * APRIL 19 - ECB President Wim Duisenberg says euro not at point where large scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed. Euro at $1.0668 \par \par \uc2  * MAY 24 - European Union finance ministers acknowledge slow growth in Italy may prevent it hitting budget deficit target of 2.0 percent of GDP in 1999. Euro closes at $1.0606 \par \par \uc2  * JUNE 3 - Serbian parliament accepts plan for peace in Kosovo. Euro closes at $1.0324 \par \par \uc2  * JUNE 8 - Bundesbank President-designate Ernst Welteke said the Ecu's (European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit) early 1998 rate of $1.08 was the appropriate reference rate for the euro, not the January 4 starting rate. Euro closes at $1.0466 \par \par \uc2  * JUNE 11 - ECB Chief Economist Otmar Issing said: "A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should never say that it will never \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It should always leave speculators uncertain about whether and when it will do so." Euro closes at $1.0517 \par \par \uc2  * JUNE 15 - Premium on 10-year U.S. interest rates over German equivalents widens to 1.79 percentage points, the widest in 10 years. Euro closes at $1.0426 * JUNE 18 - Bank of Japan bought euros for yen, using the ECB as its agent. It was the first time the ECB had been involved in any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  exercise. Euro closes at $1.0395 \par \par \uc2  * JUNE 21 - European Commission President-designate Romano Prodi said it would be difficult for Italy to remain in the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the long term if inflation continued to erode its competitiveness. Euro closes at $1.0351 \par \par \uc2  * JUNE 30 - U.S. Federal Reserve raises target fed funds rate a quarter-point to 5.0 percent. Euro closes at $1.0357. \par \par \uc2  * AUGUST 24 - U.S. Federal Reserve raises target fed funds rate a quarter-point to 5.25 percent. Euro closes at $1.0543. \par \par \uc2  * AUGUST 27 - Dow sheds one percent after U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan says the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should pay more attention to the prices of equities and other assets when setting interest rates. Euro closes at $1.0463. \par \par \uc2  * SEPTEMBER 7 - Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke said he saw $1.05 as an appropriate exchange rate for the euro as it did not pose a threat to internal price stability. The euro closes at $1.0587 \par \par \uc2  * NOVEMBER 2 - French Finance Minister Dominque Strauss-Kahn resigns. Euro closes at $1.0518. \par \par \uc2  * NOVEMBER 4 - European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raises interest rates by a half-percentage point. Euro closes at $1.0376. \par \par \uc2  * NOVEMBER 16 - U.S. Federal Reserve raises target fed funds rate quarter-point to 5.50 percent. Euro closes at $1.0295. \par \par \uc2  * NOVEMBER 26 - German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to save construction giant Phillip Holzmann AG from insolvency. Move sparks criticism about Europe's ability to reform corporate sector. Germany also tried to block a hostile takeover bid for Mannesmann AG. Euro closes week at $1.0164. \par \par \uc2  * NOVEMBER 29 - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly to try and stem the yen's rise against the dollar and the euro. Dealers see the BoJ as isolated in its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts. \par \par \uc2  * NOVEMBER 29 - ECB President Wim Duisenberg testifies before the European Parliament and says \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a potential weapon but gives no hints such a move is planned. Euro closes at $1.0093. \par \par \uc2  * DECEMBER 2 - ECB President Wim Duisenberg says euro has strong potential to appreciate, euro falls to one-for-one with the U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  ((-U.S. Financial Markets (212) 859-1660 - )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc208v7u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
