\par\par \b \uc2  Ex-MOF Sakakibara: Think Highly Of BOJ Statement \b0\par\par\uc2 177 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1999\par 09:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Nikkei/Dow Jones)--A former top official at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned Wednesday that if nothing more is done to keep the yen from rising, the nation's economic recovery will be delayed. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, former vice finance minister for international affairs, also said in a speech that "some sort of further easing" is "extremely important." \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara was speaking after the Bank of Japan took the unusual step of releasing a statement attesting to its desire to work with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen from strengthening. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara also said that he thinks highly of the statement issued by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Masaru Hayami Wednesday morning. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the strongest impact when it is linked with macroeconomic measures," Sakakibara said. \par \par \uc2  He added, "Cooperation between the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is key for requesting U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets." \par \par \uc2  Around 0956 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y102.30 and the euro was trading at Y103.60. \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvc1088qj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
