\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ: Hayami Statement Refers To Unsterilized  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1999\par 02:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a bid to explain a statement issued earlier, said Wednesday that market players shouldn't look at excess reserve amounts as a signal of policy change. \par \par \uc2  In a briefing, a BOJ official said the current amount of excess reserves routinely left in the money market - Y1 trillion - is plenty and the BOJ won't change that. \par \par \uc2  The official also said that policy currently being carried out by the BOJ represents a defacto unsterilization of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some overseas players appear to misunderstand the concept of unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the official said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ is conducting policy with the aim of easing yen strength, the official said. \par \par \uc2  If term rates - interest rates on debt with maturities of less than a year - move higher, then the BOJ could increase the amount of excess reserves left in the money market, the official said. \par \par \uc2  The official was briefing reporters after Governor Masaru Hayami issued a statement earlier in the day. That statement read in full: \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan supports the recent action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and strongly hopes that market stability is restored as soon as possible. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank is prepared to promptly provide sufficient funds in order to maintain the stability of the short-term money market, taking account of the government's yen funding of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and any disruptive impact of excessive movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on domestic financial transactions." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Bank has been flexibly providing ample funds to the short-term\par money market taking account of factors including yen liquidity arising\par from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and, under this \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par framework, today continued to supply substantial amount of liquidity."\par -0- 01/12/99 01-37G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvc10887l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
