\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar falters as BOJ easing talk fades. \b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1999\par 08:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 1 (Reuters) - The dollar, boosted earlier on Wednesday by speculation the Bank of Japan may ease its monetary policy, gave up much of its modest gains by late afternoon as such talk receded. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ had not been detected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday by selling yen for dollars, but wariness the BOJ again may do so was supporting the greenback, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Respite for the dollar, which is down over four percent from last week's high of 106.60 yen, is likely to be short-lived, traders added. \par \par \uc2  "Hopes for a recovery in the Japanese economy and demand for yen to invest in Japanese stocks remains strong. The trend is toward a stronger yen," said Yasuharu Tsuru, manager for Mitsubishi Trust and Banking Corp. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar stood at 102.11/19\tab   yen as of 0606 GMT against 102.12 yen in late U.S. trading on Tuesday.\par The euro\tab   stood at $1.0094/99 against $1.0089 in late U.S. trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier on Wednesday, the dollar received a slight boost from an ambiguous statement by Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami, which prompted speculation of a further easing in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the end, comments by a senior BOJ official quashed speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had decided to further ease its monetary policy, forcing the greenback into retreat.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At its regular 0020 GMT money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Bank of Japan left the money market with a fund surplus of 1.0 trillion yen, unchanged from Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders initially took the unchanged surplus to mean the BOJ had decided to sterilise Monday's yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Masaru Hayami's statement, which was released short afterwards, caused some confusion in the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The statement said: "The Bank of Japan is prepared to provide sufficient funds in order to maintain the stability of the short-term money market, taking account of the government's yen funding of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hayami's statement fuelled speculation that the BOJ may have decided to unsterilise Monday's yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and boosted the dollar to an intraday high of 102.55 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think the BOJ Governor may have purposely used vague wording in order to increase the effectiveness of the bank's (recent) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Mamoru Yamazaki, senior economist for Paribas Capital Markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But in practice, it is very difficult to gauge whether or not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been sterilised, and it is questionable whether such distinctions matter," Yamazaki said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Later, Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda praised the BOJ governor's statement for supporting the MOF's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the dollar was dragged off its intraday high as a senior BOJ official clarified the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's position.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Izumi Yamashita, director of the BOJ's financial markets department, said in a briefing to reporters: "Our zero interest rate policy is effective in mitigating the yen's rise."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He added that the whole argument of whether or not to sterilise \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was meaningless under the zero interest rate policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Looking forward, dealers said they expected the yen to gain more ground against the dollar in coming weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The release next Monday of July-September gross domestic product data, and of the BOJ's "tankan" corporate survey the following week, could be catalysts for the dollar's fall below 100 yen, Mitsubishi Trust's Tsuru said. ((Masayuki Kitano, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473 3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0704 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Graphics, with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab US Close   Last\tab Pct Change  YTD %\par \tab \tab 30 Nov.\par \tab \tab   1.0089     1.0098\tab +0.09     -13.85\par \tab \tab   102.12     102.06\tab -0.06     -13.85\par \tab \tab   103.04     103.10\tab +0.06\tab -9.84\par \tab \tab   1.5871     1.5856\tab -0.09     +15.44\par \tab \tab   1.5984     1.5976\tab -0.05\tab -3.40\par \tab \tab   1.4736     1.4738\tab +0.01\tab -3.64\par \tab \tab   0.6351     0.6368\tab +0.27\tab +4.14\par \tab \tab   1.6022     1.6016\tab -0.04\tab -0.64\par \tab \tab   0.6305     0.6315\tab +0.16     -10.06.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc1091wx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
