\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar wobbly vs yen amid caution over BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 775 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1999\par 04:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 1 (Reuters) - The dollar wobbled near 102 yen in Wednesday morning trade in Tokyo as the market remained cautious about the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third consecutive day to curb the yen's advance. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By 0212 GMT, the greenback\tab   stood at 102.20/25 yen, up from 102.12 yen late Tuesday in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "The market is nervous because \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can occur at any time at these levels," said a dealer at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar dipped temporarily to 101.99 yen after hopes faded that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not sterilise Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by leaving the yen it sold in the market. \par \par \uc2  Japanese exporters and investors and foreign players were seen eager to sell the dollar at above 102.50 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At its regular 0020 GMT money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BOJ left a daily surplus of 1.0 trillion yen, unchanged from the previous day, indicating that it had sterilised Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Settlements of spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions are made two business days after they are conducted. \par \par \uc2  Shigeyasu Kobayashi, a chief manager of Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, said the BOJ's action was expected by domestic players, but some foreign players had hoped the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would leave the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised. \par \par \uc2  In an unusual statement issued after the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported the actions by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF). \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan supports the recent action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and strongly hopes that market stability is restored as soon as possible," the statement said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar briefly rose to a high of 102.55 yen in morning trade as parts of Hayami's comments were misinterpreted in a local television report. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened after NHK mistakingly reported that the BOJ had adopted a new credit easing method through unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At a BOJ briefing held in late morning, a BOJ official reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance that it could not agree with the view that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be ineffective if sterilised. \par \par \uc2  In addition, Izumi Yamashita, director of the BOJ's Financial Markets Department, said the present policy of pumping funds into the money market to guide short-term rates to zero was helping the government weaken the yen, Jiji news agency reported. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that after testing the topside, the greenback was now likely to gradually slide to try the lower end, possibly prompting the BOJ to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. \par \par \uc2  They said Japanese exporters had lowered their yen-buying levels to around 102.50-103.00 to the dollar, while foreign players were eager to buy yen to invest in Japanese government bonds. \par \par \uc2  "Even if interest rates are rock bottom, foreigners can still gain from the strength of the yen against the euro and the dollar," another Japanese city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was likely to test the four-year low of 101.25 marked last Friday after trying psychological support at around 101.50 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also seen powerful against the euro, with Japanese investors keen to sell the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for yen, they said. \par \par \uc2  By 0304 GMT, the euro was quoted at 103.24/37 yen against 103.04 in late New York. The euro hit a fresh life low of 102.23 yen overnight. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the 11-month old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood at $1.0097/02 from $1.0089 in late New York trade after euro-supportive comments from European officials curbed aggressive selling. ((Ayumi Moriyama, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8550 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0308GMT.  All data taken from Reuters with \par \par \uc2  percentage change calculated from the daily U.S. close at \par \par \uc2  2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab     Last   US Close  % Chg   YTD %   1998 Close\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 30 Nov.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0097   1.0089   +0.08   -13.86   1.1721\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      102.21   102.12   +0.09   -13.86   113.20\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     103.22   103.04   +0.17    -9.71   131.84\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.5859   1.5871   -0.08   +15.46   1.3735\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5985   1.5984   +0.01    -3.35   1.6539\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4745   1.4736   +0.06    -3.60   1.5295\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6354   0.6351   +0.05    +3.91   0.6115\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.